,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.336869681,"data":"       | Goal: maximize min(b + w). This is similar to bipartite assignment problem: we have two sets of cells (black and white) with degrees. We need to assign numbers to each set to maximize minimal sum across edges. Since each black cell is adjacent to at least 2 white cells (corners) and up to 4. So the minimal sum will be determined by the smallest black number plus the smallest white number among its neighbors. If we can ensure that the smallest black number is paired only with relatively large white numbers, maybe we can raise minimal sum beyond 1802.\n"}
