,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.340526599,"data":"       | But we need to verify if S=3600 is possible. Upper bound: Since smallest number 1 must have neighbor at least 3599 (since 1+3599=3600). There is exactly one 3599 and one 3600. If 1 is placed at a corner (degree 2), we need two neighbors each \u003e= 3599. But we have only two numbers \u003e= 3599: 3599 and 3600. So we can assign them as the two neighbors. That works.\n"}
