,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.340534097,"data":"       | Let's compute needed counts: For each number k, we need at least degree(k) neighbors each \u003e= S - k. But neighbors can be shared between multiple small numbers (a high number can be neighbor to multiple small numbers). So we need to allocate high numbers to serve as neighbors for many small numbers.\n"}
