,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.340540387,"data":"       | But note: high numbers themselves also have constraints: they need neighbors that are at least S - high number, which may be small. Since S=3600, for a high number h close to 3600, S - h is small (e.g., for 3600, S - 3600 = 0, no constraint). So high numbers have no lower bound on neighbor values (since they are already large). So they can be placed anywhere, even adjacent to each other.\n"}
