,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.340550395,"data":"       | But is there any obstacle? Let's attempt to construct algorithmically for 60x60 using heuristics: assign numbers to cells such that each edge sum \u003e= 3600. Use greedy algorithm: start with empty grid, assign numbers from smallest to largest, placing each small number at a cell where all already placed neighbors satisfy sum \u003e=3600 (i.e., neighbor numbers \u003e= 3600 - small number). Since we place small numbers early, we need to ensure there are enough high numbers later to fill neighbor cells.\n"}
