,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.343798279,"data":"       | Let’s order cells by degree: 4 corners degree2, 232 edge cells degree3, 3364 interior degree4.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.343799509,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.343800571,"data":"       | Suppose we assign numbers 1..a to corners (a \u003c= 4). Then each of those numbers has degree 2, requiring their neighbors to be at least S - value. Since each neighbor may be shared between two low numbers, we need to ensure enough high numbers.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.343802063,"data":"       | \n"}
