,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344267859,"data":"       | analysisStill heavy. Maybe S=16 is impossible and proof may rely on parity or counting.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344269079,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344270134,"data":"       | Consider that sum of all numbers is 136. For each edge, sum \u003e=16, total edge sum \u003e= 16*24 = 384. But total edge sum is fixed as Σ value*deg. Let's compute minimal possible total edge sum given S=16? Actually we need to see if we can achieve total edge sum \u003e=384. Let's compute the maximum possible total edge sum (we already computed as 456). So 384 is less than 456, so not contradictory.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344271959,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.34427299,"data":"       | But maybe we can use inequality: For each cell with value v, the sum of its incident edge sums includes v deg(v) times, each edge sum \u003e= S, so total edge sum \u003e= S*E. But each edge counted twice in sum of incident edge sums. Actually total edge sum = Σ_{edges} (a+b) = Σ_{cells} v*deg(v). So condition edge sum \u003e= S for each edge implies Σ_{cells} v*deg(v) \u003e= S*E. That's same as earlier bound.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344274902,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344275925,"data":"       | But we can also bound Σ_{cells} v*deg(v) from above (max) as we computed 456. So S \u003c= floor(456/24)=19. Not enough.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344277269,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344278276,"data":"       | Thus S=16 not ruled out.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344279362,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344280392,"data":"       | Maybe we can prove S_max = N - 1 for even N? For 4x4, N=16, max S=15 = N-1. For 2x2, N=4, max S=4 = N? Actually N=4, N-1=3, but max S=4 \u003e N-1. So not consistent.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344281737,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344283012,"data":"       | For 3x3, N=9, max S=9 = N. So maybe for odd N, max S = N, for even N, max S = N-1? Let's test with 2x2 (even) gave S=4 = N, not N-1. So pattern not consistent.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344284327,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344285347,"data":"       | But maybe for n \u003e=4 even, max S = N-1? Let's test with 4x4 we think 15 (N-1). Let's test 6x6 (N=36) using heuristic to see approximate max S. Use simulated annealing to try to achieve S=36? maybe 35? Let's try.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344286765,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344287777,"data":"       | assistantanalysis to=python codedef random_grid(m,n):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344288909,"data":"       |     N=m*n\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344289963,"data":"       |     perm=list(range(1,N+1))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344291052,"data":"       |     random.shuffle(perm)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344292123,"data":"       |     return [perm[i*n:(i+1)*n for i in range(m)]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344293232,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.34429425,"data":"       | def simulated_target(m,n,target,iterations=200000):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344296969,"data":"       |     grid=random_grid(m,n)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344298072,"data":"       |     best=min_edge_sum_grid(grid)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344299183,"data":"       |     best_grid=[row[:] for row in grid]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344300292,"data":"       |     for it in range(iterations):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344301376,"data":"       |         i1,j1=random.randrange(m),random.randrange(n)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344302496,"data":"       |         i2,j2=random.randrange(m),random.randrange(n)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344303624,"data":"       |         grid[i1][j1],grid[i2][j2]=grid[i2][j2],grid[i1][j1]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344304762,"data":"       |         cur=min_edge_sum_grid(grid)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344305852,"data":"       |         if cur\u003ebest:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344306936,"data":"       |             best=cur\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344308029,"data":"       |             best_grid=[row[:] for row in grid]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344309139,"data":"       |             if best\u003e=target:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344310252,"data":"       |                 return best,best_grid\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344311352,"data":"       |         # accept if not worse with probability\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344312462,"data":"       |         if cur\u003e=best:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344313559,"data":"       |             accept=True\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344314612,"data":"       |         else:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344315669,"data":"       |             accept=False\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344316752,"data":"       |         if not accept:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344317814,"data":"       |             grid[i1][j1],grid[i2][j2]=grid[i2][j2],grid[i1][j1]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.344318985,"data":"       |     return best,best_grid\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.34432005,"data":"       | \n"}
