,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.346130705,"data":"       | analysisWe need to find maximum possible minimal sum of two adjacent cells in a 60x60 grid filled with numbers 1..3600 (each used exactly once). We want to maximize S such that for any arrangement, the minimal sum over all adjacent pairs is at least S. Equivalent to find arrangement that maximizes the minimum sum of adjacent cells. This is a combinatorial optimization (maximin). We need to find the maximum possible S (i.e., the largest value such that there exists a filling where every adjacent pair sum \u003e= S). We need to compute that value.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.346132711,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.346133768,"data":"       | We need to think about constraints. The grid has 60x60 cells, adjacency edges: horizontal edges: 60 rows * 59 columns = 60*59 = 3540. Vertical edges: 59 rows * 60 columns = 3540. Total edges = 7080 adjacent pairs (undirected). For each edge, sum of the two numbers must be \u003e= S. We want to maximize S.\n"}
