,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.346172659,"data":"       | Thus we can derive an upper bound on S using the minimal possible weighted sum given the degree distribution. Since we can arrange numbers arbitrarily, we can try to minimize weighted sum for a given S? Wait we want to maximize S such that there exists arrangement meeting condition. So we can find an upper bound on S using inequality: For any arrangement, the weighted sum (sum deg*value) is fixed? No, deg*value depends on arrangement because value assigned to each cell influences weighted sum. But we can bound weighted sum from below based on values and degrees.\n"}
