,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.347172383,"data":"       | Observation: For grid graph, we can color cells black/white. Adjacent pairs are black-white. The sum condition only involves cross-color pairs. So we can think of labeling each color set with numbers. The minimal sum across edges is min_{(b,w) edge} (b + w). Since each black cell connects to up to 4 whites, the minimal sum will be at least min_{b} (b + min_{w neighbor of b} w). So we can attempt to maximize this by arranging numbers such that each black cell's neighboring whites are relatively large, and each white cell's neighboring blacks are relatively large.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.347174382,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.347175788,"data":"       | Potential strategy: Sort numbers and assign them to cells in a \"checkerboard\" pattern but not simply halves; we can intermix to increase minimal sum.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.347177141,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.347178188,"data":"       | Consider ordering numbers ascending and assign them to cells in a snake pattern such that each low number is surrounded by high numbers. Since each low number has up to 4 neighbors, we need at least 4 high numbers for each low number. So we need enough high numbers to serve as neighbors for low numbers.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.347181465,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.347182543,"data":"       | Define threshold t: numbers \u003c= t are \"low\". For each low number, we need at least degree(v) high numbers \u003e= S - v. However high numbers can be shared among multiple low numbers (since a high number can be adjacent to up to 4 low numbers). So the capacity condition: sum_{low cells} degree(low) \u003c= sum_{high cells} degree(high). Since each edge connects low-high (cannot have low-low if S \u003e 2t). For S \u003e 2t, low cells cannot be adjacent to each other. So the bipartite graph induced must be a cut. So we need to partition cells into low set L and high set H such that all edges are between L and H (i.e., L is independent set). The maximum size of independent set in grid is 1800 (half). So |L| \u003c= 1800. So we can have up to 1800 low numbers.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.347185073,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.347186119,"data":"       | Now we also need degree capacity: each low cell degree d_i (2,3,4). The total degree of low cells D_L = sum d_i. Each edge incident to low cell connects to a high cell, counting toward D_H (degree of high cells) as well. Since each edge counted twice (once for each endpoint), D_L = D_H = total number of edges *2? Wait each edge contributes degree 1 to each endpoint. So sum of degrees over all cells = 2E = 2*7080 = 14160. So D_L + D_H = 14160. If we choose L independent set, edges only between L and H, then each edge contributes 1 to D_L and 1 to D_H, so D_L = D_H = E = 7080. Indeed if L is independent set and covers half vertices, then each edge has one endpoint in L and one in H, thus D_L = D_H = number of edges = 7080.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.347188352,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.347189539,"data":"       | Thus if we can select L of size 1800 such that sum of degrees of L equals 7080. Since each interior cell degree 4, edge cell degree 3, corner degree 2. Need to select 1800 cells with total degree 7080. Average degree = 7080/1800 = 3.933... So we need mostly interior cells (degree 4) and some edge cells to reduce average to 3.933.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.347191147,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.347192175,"data":"       | Compute number of interior cells needed: Suppose x interior (deg4), y edge (deg3), z corner (deg2). x+y+z = 1800. Total degree = 4x+3y+2z = 7080.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.347193478,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.3471945,"data":"       | We also know there are only 4 corners total, so z \u003c=4. Edge cells total 232, interior 3364.\n"}
