,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.348289984,"data":"       | Check: 4 + 232 + 3364 = 3600.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.348291058,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.348292443,"data":"       | Now we want to assign numbers 1..3600 to cells to maximize sum of degree*value. This is a classic rearrangement inequality: assign largest numbers to highest degrees.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.348293787,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.348294824,"data":"       | Thus assign largest 3364 numbers to interior cells (degree 4), next largest 232 numbers to edge cells (degree 3), smallest 4 numbers to corners (degree 2). That maximizes total weighted sum.\n"}
