,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.350276174,"data":"       | Thus an upper bound for S is floor(total edge sum / E). Since total edge sum is known given arrangement? Wait total edge sum depends on arrangement because degree weighting. But sum_i a_i * deg_i is fixed? deg_i are fixed per position, but arrangement changes which numbers are placed at which degree positions. So total edge sum depends on assignment of numbers to cells with different degrees.\n"}
