,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.350482656,"data":"       | Better: Use Latin-style pattern: assign numbers such that each row is decreasing from left to right, and each column decreasing from top to bottom? That would place small numbers at top-left corner and large numbers at bottom-right, ensuring that any adjacent pair sum maybe large enough? Let's test small grid with such monotone decreasing property: assign numbers decreasing both right and down (i.e., numbers decreasing as we move right or down). Then any adjacent pair includes a larger number (right or down neighbor) and a smaller number (left/up neighbor). The sum might be at least something.\n"}
