,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.351363708,"data":"       | Thus we can use Hall's marriage theorem to bound S: For any subset X of black cells, the set of white cells that can serve as neighbor must be at least |X| (by capacity). The size of neighbor set is limited by number of white cells with numbers \u003e= S - max_{a in X} a? Not.\n"}
