,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.351736311,"data":"       | Let’s denote the graph G = grid 60x60. There are V = 3600 vertices, E = edges = (60-1)*60*2 = 59*60*2 = 7080? Actually compute: horizontal edges: rows 60, each row has 59 horizontal edges =\u003e 60*59 = 3540. vertical edges: columns 60, each column has 59 vertical edges =\u003e also 3540. Total edges = 7080.\n"}
