,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.351758189,"data":"       | Potential approach: treat as a matching problem: For each edge, we want sum \u003e= S. Equivalent to: For each vertex v, all its incident edges must have sum \u003e= S. So for each vertex v with label a = f(v), we need for each neighbor u, a + f(u) \u003e= S =\u003e f(u) \u003e= S - a. Therefore, for a given vertex v, all its neighbors must have labels at least S - a. This gives constraints.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.351759988,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.351761033,"data":"       | Thus for each vertex with label a, we need that there are at least deg(v) numbers \u003e= S - a among the labels assigned to its neighbors. Since neighbors are distinct vertices, they must have distinct numbers.\n"}
