,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.351768416,"data":"       | Perhaps we can find upper bound on S via counting arguments: Suppose we want minimal sum \u003e= S. Then for any edge, the sum of two labels \u003e= S. So the sum of all labels over edges (each edge counted once) \u003e= S * E. But sum over edges of (label of endpoint) = sum over vertices (label * degree). Because each vertex contributes its label to each incident edge. So total sum across edges = sum_{v} f(v) * deg(v). So we have:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.351770238,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.351771274,"data":"       | ∑_{v} f(v) * deg(v) \u003e= S * E.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.351772435,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.351773493,"data":"       | Thus S \u003c= (∑ f(v) deg(v)) / E.\n"}
