,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.351775707,"data":"       | We can compute RHS for any labeling; to maximize S, we need to maximize this ratio, but labeling influences sum weighted by degree. Since deg(v) are fixed (2 for corners, 3 for edges, 4 for interior). Weighted sum is ∑ a_i * deg_i. To maximize ratio, we want larger numbers assigned to higher degree vertices (since they are multiplied by larger degree). So to maximize lower bound, we assign largest numbers to interior (deg=4), medium to edge (deg=3), smallest to corners (deg=2). This is intuitive.\n"}
