,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.351968739,"data":"       | We can try to model as bipartite assignment: low vertices (set L) need neighbor slots (each low vertex has degree d slots) to be filled with high numbers (set H) such that each high number can occupy up to its own degree slots (since a high number can be adjacent to at most 4 low numbers). Actually each high vertex can serve as neighbor to at most its degree number of low vertices (if all its neighbors are low). But high vertex may also neighbor other high vertices, using up some slots.\n"}
