,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.351982381,"data":"       | If we assign the smallest low numbers to cells with smallest degree (corners) to reduce number of high neighbors needed. And assign largest high numbers to cells adjacent to many low cells.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.351985228,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.351986283,"data":"       | Thus we can treat the problem as we have two color classes of equal size (1800 each). Let L = set of low numbers (some numbers) placed on one color (say white). H = set of high numbers placed on black. We need to choose which numbers go to L and H to maximize minimal sum across edges.\n"}
