,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352058702,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352059723,"data":"       | Better to think: we need to select 1800 numbers for H; we can choose any subset of size 1800. To maximize min(L)+min(H), we want to maximize the smaller of the two minima? Actually min sum = min(L) + min(H_adjacent_to_that_min(L)). Since each low vertex's neighbors are all high vertices, the minimal sum will be min(L) + min of H among the neighbors of that low vertex. The worst low vertex will be the one with smallest label (call a_min) and its neighbors' minimal high label (call b_min). So we need to maximize a_min + b_min.\n"}
