,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352062812,"data":"       | Thus we want to maximize the smallest low label (a_min) and also ensure that the low vertex with that label has neighbors with high labels as high as possible (b_min). Since we can place a_min at a corner (degree 2) and assign its two neighbor high cells with highest possible numbers. So b_min can be as high as we can allocate.\n"}
