,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352145088,"data":"       | We need to compute number of cells of each parity: For a 60x60 board, each color has 1800 cells. Among them, corners distribution: 2 corners each color.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352146384,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352147414,"data":"       | Edge cells (non-corner) along border: total edge cells non-corner = 232. Half of them are white (since alternating). So each color has 116 edge cells (degree 3). The rest interior cells = 1800 - 2 - 116 = 1682 interior cells (degree 4) per color.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352148951,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352150026,"data":"       | Thus low side has: 2 corners (deg2), 116 edge (deg3), 1682 interior (deg4). Total low vertices = 1800.\n"}
