,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352155845,"data":"       | Similarly, high side (black) will have remaining numbers.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352157004,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352158062,"data":"       | Now we can compute required minima for each black vertex: For each black vertex, its adjacent low vertices have certain low numbers; the required minimum for the black vertex is max_{adjacent low a} (t - a). Since we want to assign a label \u003e= that. The higher the adjacent low numbers, the lower the required minimum (since t - a smaller). So to make black vertices feasible, we would like the adjacent low numbers to be as large as possible (i.e., assign larger low numbers to cells adjacent to many black vertices). However low numbers are fixed.\n"}
