,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352165628,"data":"       | Implementation steps:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352166721,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352167784,"data":"       | - Create 60x60 grid with parity (i+j) % 2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352168896,"data":"       | - Determine low color (choose parity 0 as low). We'll assign low numbers to that color.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352170123,"data":"       | - Generate list of low cells sorted by degree (2,3,4). Within same degree, any order.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352171311,"data":"       | - Assign low numbers 1..1800 accordingly.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352172421,"data":"       | - Then compute for each high cell (parity 1) the required minimum label = max(t - a_adj) over its adjacent low cells.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352173688,"data":"       | - Then we need to assign distinct integers from 1801..3600 to high cells, each \u003e= required minimum. This is a feasibility of assigning numbers to satisfy lower bounds.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352175025,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352176142,"data":"       | We can check if there exists a bijection meeting lower bounds. This is similar to checking if we can assign numbers in increasing order to cells sorted by required minima: assign smallest available number that meets requirement to each cell, ensuring distinctness. Since we have exactly as many numbers as cells, the necessary and sufficient condition is that after sorting required minima ascending, the i-th smallest required minimum \u003c= the i-th smallest available number (i.e., 1801 + i -1). This is a classic Hall-like condition for assignment with lower bounds (since any higher numbers are also okay). The condition for existence of injection from required minima to numbers is that the sorted minima are not greater than the corresponding numbers.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352178471,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352179524,"data":"       | Thus we can test feasibility for a given t.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352180654,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352181704,"data":"       | Let's implement binary search for maximal t.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352184478,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352185464,"data":"       | assistantanalysis to=python codedef max_t():\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352188021,"data":"       |     n=60\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352189071,"data":"       |     N=n*n\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352190068,"data":"       |     # parity 0 low, 1 high\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352191089,"data":"       |     low_parity=0\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352192094,"data":"       |     # compute degree for each cell\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352193145,"data":"       |     deg=[[0]*n for _ in range(n)]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352194176,"data":"       |     for i in range(n):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352195182,"data":"       |         for j in range(n):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352196376,"data":"       |             d=0\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352197411,"data":"       |             if i\u003e0: d+=1\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352198482,"data":"       |             if i\u003cn-1: d+=1\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352199544,"data":"       |             if j\u003e0: d+=1\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352200591,"data":"       |             if j\u003cn-1: d+=1\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352201666,"data":"       |             deg[i][j]=d\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352202668,"data":"       |     # list low cells\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352203685,"data":"       |     low_cells=[]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352204682,"data":"       |     high_cells=[]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.352205704,"data":"       |     for i in range(n):\n"}
