,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.353986522,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":18877.353987631,"data":"       | But white squares also are adjacent to each other? No, white squares are only adjacent to black squares, not to each other (grid bipartite). So edges only between opposite colors. So there is never an edge between two high numbers (both white) or two low numbers (both black). Good! So we can separate low and high sets onto opposite colors.\n"}
