,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.700550308,"data":"       | analysisThe search found a solution with m=8 dominoes. It didn't find any solution with fewer than 8 (since best m=8). Let's verify if there might be solution with 7 or less but not found due to search pruning maybe incomplete.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.700551774,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.700553144,"data":"       | We used recursion with heuristic picking required cell with minimal options. Should explore all possibilities given pruning bound. The lower bound used ceil(|R|/2). That is valid: each new domino can cover at most 2 required cells. So if we have required cells count \u003e 2*(best_m - current_m -1) maybe prune incorrectly? Actually we prune when current_m + lower \u003e= best_m. Since best_m currently 8, lower bound may prune some branches that could lead to solution with 7 if lower bound is too optimistic? Wait lower bound is ceil(|R|/2). That's a lower bound on additional dominoes needed to cover required cells, but there may be additional constraints that require more dominoes, not fewer. So using lower bound is safe for pruning: if even the optimistic lower bound already makes total \u003e= best_m, we can prune because we cannot beat best_m. That's fine.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.700555731,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.700556764,"data":"       | Thus search should find any solution with m \u003c 8 if exists.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.700557968,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.700559028,"data":"       | But we started with each placement as first domino. Could there be solution with zero dominoes? Not considered. But we need at least one.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.700560341,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.70056138,"data":"       | Thus minimal m appears to be 8.\n"}
