,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.701240609,"data":"       | Better approach: Consider board edges: each domino placed not touching board edge on a side must have a neighbor domino on that side. So each side not adjacent to board edge creates a \"requirement\" that must be satisfied by another domino. Count total number of such side requirements.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.701243432,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.701245027,"data":"       | Let each domino have up to 2 side requirements (if both sides not at board edge). If a side is at board edge, no requirement. So total number of side requirements = sum over dominoes of (2 - number of sides at board edge). Since board edges are limited, we can bound minimal number of dominoes.\n"}
