,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.701277529,"data":"       | Each neighbor requirement must be satisfied by a cell occupied by some domino. Each occupied cell can satisfy at most how many neighbor requirements? As earlier, each cell can be neighbor for up to 2 dominoes (one on each side along the line). But a cell belongs to a domino; that domino occupies two cells, each can be neighbor for up to 2 dominoes, so each domino can satisfy up to 4 neighbor requirements (as earlier). However note that a neighbor requirement is associated with a specific side of a domino; the cell that satisfies it is the adjacent cell (which belongs to some domino). That domino may also have its own neighbor requirements.\n"}
