,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.701318288,"data":"       | Our solution with 8 dominoes uses 8 dominoes and occupies 16 cells. No extra cells beyond domino cells (since all neighbor cells are occupied by other dominoes). So total occupied cells = 2m = 16. So we achieved perfect overlap: all neighbor cells are already domino cells. So minimal possible m must satisfy that we can arrange dominoes such that all neighbor cells are domino cells (no extra cells). That is possible for m=8 as we found.\n"}
