,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.701450523,"data":"       | Let's attempt to compute minimal m via integer programming using pulp? Not available. But we can brute force search for m up to 7 using backtracking enumerating placements. Our earlier search started with each placement as first domino and recursively placed more until R empty. It found best m=8. Did it explore all possibilities up to 7? Yes, because it pruned only when lower bound \u003e= best_m (which initially best_m=1000). So it would explore all possibilities up to any m until it found solution with m=8, then lower bound pruned branches that cannot beat 8. However after finding solution with m=8, it may prune branches where lower bound \u003e=8, i.e., lower bound \u003e=8. For m=7, lower bound = ceil(|R|/2). If |R| \u003e= 16, lower bound \u003e=8, prune. But maybe there are configurations with |R| small enough that lower bound \u003c8, but still m=7 not possible. The search would explore them.\n"}
