,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.701898594,"data":"       | We can try to search for minimal m using Python's `itertools.combinations` for small m. For each combination of placements, check constraints quickly. Since we need minimal m, we can start from low m and increase until feasible.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.701900009,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.701901054,"data":"       | But number of combinations grows quickly: C(84, m). For m=5, C(84,5) ~ 2.5e7, too many. But we can prune using non-overlap: we can generate placements that are non-overlapping using backtracking.\n"}
