,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.702016056,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.702017346,"data":"       | Given board size 7x7, we can treat each cell as either empty or occupied by a domino. Since each domino occupies two cells, we can think of tiling partially.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.702018691,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.702020868,"data":"       | We can search for minimal m using recursive backtracking: place dominos one by one, ensuring constraints for already placed dominos are satisfied (or at least not violated). However constraints involve future placements: a domino may need support cells that are not yet occupied; we can postpone checking until later. But we need to guarantee final configuration satisfies all.\n"}
