,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.703839446,"data":"       | analysisIt says solution found for m=1, which is impossible because a single domino cannot be blocked on all sides (some direction will be free). Our algorithm incorrectly treats outside board as automatically satisfied (which is correct) but also for a single domino, its required cells may be empty but we treat them as unsatisfied because they are not covered. Wait unsatisfied checks if required set is subset of occupied cells. For a single domino, occupied cells are its two cells. Required cells are outside board cells (excluded) and adjacent cells inside board. For a corner horizontal domino, required cells: right cell (0,2) and down cells (1,0),(1,1). These are not occupied, so unsatisfied should be non-empty, thus solution should not be found. However our required_cells function for horizontal includes up shift and down shift always if r+1 \u003c N (which is true for any row except bottom). For top row r=0, down shift adds cells (1,c_left) and (1,c_left+1). That's correct. So unsatisfied should be non-empty.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.703842055,"data":"       | \n"}
