,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.704679625,"data":"       | Thus any configuration with 24 dominos leaves one empty cell. That empty cell may be required for some domino's shift, causing unsatisfied. So maybe we need 24 dominos but also need to ensure the empty cell is not required by any domino. Is that possible? Possibly if empty cell is isolated such that no domino requires it. Let's test.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.704681145,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.704682107,"data":"       | We need to find a placement of 24 dominos covering 48 cells, leaving one empty cell, such that for each domino, all its required cells are occupied (i.e., either outside board or occupied). The empty cell must not be in any required set of any domino.\n"}
