,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.704684455,"data":"       | Thus we need to find a placement where the empty cell is not adjacent to any domino in a way that would be required. Let's think: For a domino, required cells are those adjacent to its ends (for shift) and the cells adjacent to its entire length (for up/down shift). So many cells around each domino are required. The empty cell would likely be required by some domino unless placed at a corner maybe? Let's test by brute force search for 24 dominos (i.e., covering all but one cell). That's a matching of size 24. Number of matchings of size 24 is huge but we can try to use algorithm to search for a configuration satisfying constraints.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.704686411,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.70468739,"data":"       | We can adapt our search to start with limit=24 and try to find solution; but our earlier search up to 24 didn't find any solution, maybe because we limited time to 5 seconds per m and visited limited; but we visited many states but maybe not enough to find solution.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.704688824,"data":"       | \n"}
