,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.706329858,"data":"       | Our search algorithm may be too aggressive in pruning: The prune condition may incorrectly prune feasible configurations if a neighbor cell is currently empty but could be occupied later by a domino that also occupies another cell that is currently empty but may later become blocked etc. Our check cell_can_be_filled ensures there exists a placement covering that cell with both cells free at current state. That seems correct: if there is no placement covering that cell without overlapping occupied cells, then that cell can never become occupied later, so direction cannot be satisfied. That's valid.\n"}
