,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.706337018,"data":"       | But we also have heuristic selection of next cell; may cause missing solutions? The algorithm explores all placements covering selected cell; but if there is a solution where some empty cells are never filled (i.e., left empty), our heuristic may still work because we only need to place m dominos; we may leave many cells empty. The algorithm selects a next cell with fewest placement options among empty cells that have at least one placement option. However if there are empty cells that have zero placement options (i.e., cannot be part of any domino due to overlapping constraints), they are ignored. That's fine.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.70633893,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.706339933,"data":"       | Thus algorithm should explore all possibilities for given m, albeit maybe large search space but we got solution for m=24 quickly, but for lower m it may take long; but we saw none up to 23 quickly (maybe due to early pruning). However we need to be sure there is indeed no solution with m\u003c24.\n"}
