,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.706348032,"data":"       | Observation: For each domino, at least 2 interior sides (if placed at corner). So total interior sides R \u003e= 2*m (if all dominos are corners). But there are only 4 corners, so at most 4 dominos can have 2 interior sides. The rest must have at least 3 interior sides (edge) or 4 interior sides (interior). Let's compute minimal possible sum of interior sides given m dominos.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.70634965,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.706350658,"data":"       | Let a = number of corner dominos (max 4). Let b = number of edge (non-corner) dominos. Let c = number of interior dominos. Then a+b+c = m.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.706351855,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.7063528,"data":"       | Corner dominos have interior sides = 2 each.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.706353833,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.706354834,"data":"       | Edge dominos (non-corner) have interior sides = 3 each (since one side is edge). Actually edge dominos could be placed such that both cells are on edge but not corner; they have exactly one side on board edge (the side outward). For a domino lying along edge, there is one side outward (edge), the opposite side interior, and the two perpendicular sides interior. So total interior sides = 3.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.706356428,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.706357404,"data":"       | Interior dominos have interior sides = 4.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.706358609,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.706359587,"data":"       | Thus total interior sides R = 2a + 3b + 4c.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.706360616,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.706361558,"data":"       | We have constraints on a,b,c based on board geometry.\n"}
