,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.70637611,"data":"       | Consider each empty cell (not occupied). Could it be adjacent to a domino side that needs blocking? If a domino side is blocked by an occupied neighbor, that neighbor cell is occupied. So each interior side corresponds to an adjacency between a domino and an occupied cell. However a single occupied cell can serve as neighbor for up to 4 sides (one per direction). So total number of interior sides ≤ 4 * (number of occupied cells). Since each occupied cell is part of a domino, number of occupied cells = 2m.\n"}
