,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.708874053,"data":"       | analysisAll false up to 24 (max). That suggests maybe there is no configuration satisfying condition? But obviously there is at least trivial configuration: fill entire board with dominoes (24 dominoes) except one cell left empty (since odd board). Does that configuration satisfy condition? Let's think: If we tile almost entire board, interior dominoes may still have empty side cells (the single empty cell). Some dominoes adjacent to empty cell may slide into it. So not locked.\n"}
