,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710800056,"data":"       | Now we need to search for minimal set of placements such that for each placement p, its neighbor cells are covered by some placement (including possibly itself? but neighbor cells are not part of its own cells). So we need O (set of occupied cells) to include all neighbor cells.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710801558,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710802598,"data":"       | Thus condition: For all p in selected placements, neigh(p) ⊆ O (occupied cells). Since O is union of cells of selected placements.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71080388,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710804921,"data":"       | Thus we need O to be a superset of union of neigh(p) over selected placements.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710806483,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710807528,"data":"       | Thus we can think of O must be closed under operation: O must contain all neighbor cells of each domino in O.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710808745,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710809784,"data":"       | Thus we can search for minimal set of placements such that O = union cells of placements, and for each placement p, neigh(p) ⊆ O.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710811086,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710812114,"data":"       | Implementation: Use recursion building set of placements S. Keep O = set of cells covered. At each step, we can compute required cells = union of neigh(p) for p in S. Must be subset of O (i.e., all required cells already covered). However we may add new placements that cover required cells later. So during building, we may have required cells not yet covered; that's okay as long as we plan to cover them later.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710813834,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710814836,"data":"       | Thus we need final condition: after we stop adding placements, required cells must be subset of O.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710816048,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710817058,"data":"       | Thus we can implement search that ensures we eventually cover all required cells.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710818227,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710819254,"data":"       | We can use algorithm similar to hitting set: we need to cover required cells.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710820415,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710821411,"data":"       | We can start with empty S, O empty, required empty.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710822574,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710825674,"data":"       | We can iteratively add placements to cover required cells.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710826866,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710827918,"data":"       | Goal: minimize |S|.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710828986,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710830018,"data":"       | We can use BFS incremental search for m from 1 upward, trying to find any solution.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710831242,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710832268,"data":"       | Given small board, we can attempt to use Python's `itertools.combinations` for small m (maybe up to 6 or 7) and test condition quickly. Let's compute number of combos for m=6: C(84,6) ~ 84^6/720 ≈ (3.0e11)/720 ≈ 4e8, too many.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710833747,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710834751,"data":"       | But we can prune using requirement that O must be closed; many combos will fail early.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710835947,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71083695,"data":"       | Better to use backtracking with heuristic.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710838043,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710839063,"data":"       | Let's implement recursive search with pruning and bound.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710840226,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710841237,"data":"       | We can also use memoization: state defined by O (occupied cells) maybe.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710842396,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710843436,"data":"       | But O can be up to 49 cells, but we can encode as bitmask of 49 bits (int). That's feasible.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710844616,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710845869,"data":"       | We can precompute for each placement its cell mask (bits for its two cells) and neighbor mask (bits for neighbor cells). Then we need to find a set of placements such that union of cell masks = O, and union of neighbor masks ⊆ O.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710847337,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710848358,"data":"       | Thus condition: (union of neighbor masks) \u0026 ~O == 0.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710849527,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710850551,"data":"       | Thus we need O to be a superset of neighbor union.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710851705,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710852732,"data":"       | Thus we can search for O that satisfies O includes neighbor union.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710853893,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710854928,"data":"       | But O must be representable as union of placements (i.e., O must be a set of cells that can be partitioned into domino pairs that correspond to placements (i.e., each pair adjacent). That's a perfect matching condition on the induced subgraph of adjacency (grid edges). So O must be a domino tilable region (i.e., each connected component must have even number of cells and there exists a perfect matching). Since we are constructing O via placements, we can just ensure we add placements.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710856773,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710857791,"data":"       | Thus we can search for O directly: find a set of cells O such that O can be tiled by dominos (i.e., there exists a set of placements covering O) and O includes neighbor cells of each domino in that tiling. Equivalent to earlier.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.7108608,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710861839,"data":"       | Thus we can search for placements directly.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710862943,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710863963,"data":"       | Let's implement backtracking:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710865067,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710866111,"data":"       | - Keep O_mask (bits of occupied cells)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710867293,"data":"       | - Keep N_mask (bits of neighbor cells required) = union of neighbor masks of placed dominos.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710868473,"data":"       | - Keep count of placed dominos.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710869564,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710870599,"data":"       | Goal: find O_mask such that N_mask ⊆ O_mask (i.e., N_mask \u0026 ~O_mask == 0) and O_mask is exactly union of placed dominos (by construction). So at termination we need N_mask ⊆ O_mask.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710872047,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710873062,"data":"       | During search, we can add a placement p if its cells are not already occupied (i.e., cell mask \u0026 O_mask == 0). Then new O_mask' = O_mask | cell_mask(p). New N_mask' = N_mask | neighbor_mask(p). Continue.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710874488,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710875699,"data":"       | We can prune: if at any point there exists a required cell (bit in N_mask) that is not in O_mask and cannot be covered by any remaining placement (i.e., no placement covering that cell without overlapping O_mask). Then prune.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710877104,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710878114,"data":"       | Also we can bound: if current count \u003e= best found, prune.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71087928,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710880293,"data":"       | We can start with best = large (maybe 10). We'll search depth-first.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710881455,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710882465,"data":"       | Let's implement.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710883556,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710884558,"data":"       | assistantanalysis to=python codefrom functools import lru_cache\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710885716,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71088674,"data":"       | n=7\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710887781,"data":"       | # map cell to bit index\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710888848,"data":"       | cell_to_bit = {(i,j): i*n + j for i in range(n) for j in range(n)}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710889996,"data":"       | def mask_of_cells(cells):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710891063,"data":"       |     m=0\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710892354,"data":"       |     for c in cells:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710893406,"data":"       |         m |= 1 \u003c\u003c cell_to_bit[c]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710894594,"data":"       |     return m\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71089566,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710896663,"data":"       | placements_masks=[]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710897739,"data":"       | for p in placements:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710900302,"data":"       |     cell_mask = mask_of_cells(p['cells'])\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710901456,"data":"       |     neigh_mask = mask_of_cells(p['neigh'])\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710902588,"data":"       |     placements_masks.append((cell_mask, neigh_mask))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710903709,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710904737,"data":"       | # Precompute for each cell, list of placement indices that cover it\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710905887,"data":"       | cell_to_placements = {c: [] for c in cell_to_bit}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710906998,"data":"       | for idx,(cell_mask, neigh_mask) in enumerate(placements_masks):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710908132,"data":"       |     # get cells from mask\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710909205,"data":"       |     # iterate bits\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710910262,"data":"       |     for i in range(n*n):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710911348,"data":"       |         if cell_mask\u003e\u003ei \u0026 1:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710912576,"data":"       |             cell = (i//n, i%n)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710913632,"data":"       |             cell_to_placements[cell].append(idx)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710914732,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710915732,"data":"       | # For quick check of possible placements covering a cell without overlapping current O\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710916891,"data":"       | def possible_placements_for_cell(cell, O_mask):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710918008,"data":"       |     # return list of placement indices that cover cell and have no overlap with O_mask\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710919163,"data":"       |     res=[]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710920238,"data":"       |     for idx in cell_to_placements[cell]:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710921329,"data":"       |         cell_mask,_ = placements_masks[idx]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710922421,"data":"       |         if cell_mask \u0026 O_mask == 0:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710923587,"data":"       |             res.append(idx)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710924643,"data":"       |     return res\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710925696,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710926696,"data":"       | best = 100\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710927744,"data":"       | best_solution = None\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710928826,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710929834,"data":"       | # order cells maybe by something\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710930906,"data":"       | all_cells = list(cell_to_bit.keys())\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710932006,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710933221,"data":"       | def dfs(O_mask, N_mask, placed, start_idx=0):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710934364,"data":"       |     global best, best_solution\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710935435,"data":"       |     # prune by count\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710936493,"data":"       |     if placed \u003e= best:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710937649,"data":"       |         return\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710938708,"data":"       |     # check if all required cells are already covered\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710941323,"data":"       |     uncovered = N_mask \u0026 ~O_mask\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710942501,"data":"       |     if uncovered == 0:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710943596,"data":"       |         # we have a valid solution (maybe we could add more dominos but we want minimal)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710944772,"data":"       |         best = placed\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710945817,"data":"       |         best_solution = O_mask\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710946991,"data":"       |         print(\"Found solution with\", placed, \"dominos\")\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710948273,"data":"       |         return\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710949329,"data":"       |     # choose a required cell that is not yet covered\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710950448,"data":"       |     # pick lowest bit\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710951516,"data":"       |     # get index of a bit in uncovered\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710952628,"data":"       |     # find cell coordinates\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710953712,"data":"       |     # we can use bit_length\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710954785,"data":"       |     # get first set bit\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710955841,"data":"       |     bit = (uncovered \u0026 -uncovered)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710957002,"data":"       |     cell_idx = (bit.bit_length() - 1)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710958109,"data":"       |     cell = (cell_idx // n, cell_idx % n)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710959209,"data":"       |     # iterate possible placements covering this cell\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710960325,"data":"       |     for idx in possible_placements_for_cell(cell, O_mask):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710961459,"data":"       |         cell_mask, neigh_mask = placements_masks[idx]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710962554,"data":"       |         # add placement\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710963633,"data":"       |         dfs(O_mask | cell_mask, N_mask | neigh_mask, placed+1)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710964784,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710965806,"data":"       | # start search\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710966849,"data":"       | dfs(0,0,0)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710967879,"data":"       | print(\"best\", best)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.710968995,"data":"       | \n"}
