,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71121669,"data":"       | Thus we can model as constraints: For each domino p and each direction d, let S(p,d) be set of cells (within board) that need to be occupied to block that direction. Then we need sum_{q covering any cell in S(p,d)} x_q ≥ x_p (since if p placed, at least one covering cell needed). Note that the covering cell could be part of p itself? For horizontal domino, left set cell is not part of p, right set not part, up set cells are not part of p (since they are above). So no overlap.\n"}
