,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712070967,"data":"       | Observation: For each domino, each direction requires at least one occupied neighbor cell. So each domino needs at least 4 neighbor cells (one per direction) but some may overlap with each other or be same cell (e.g., up neighbor set may share cells with left neighbor set of another domino). So minimal total occupied cells may be less than 2*m + 4*m.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712072626,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71207364,"data":"       | We can attempt to find lower bound using counting arguments.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712074794,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712076153,"data":"       | Consider each domino contributes 2 cells. For each direction, we need at least one occupied cell among a set of size 1 (for left/right) or 2 (for up/down). So each domino requires at least 4 occupied neighbor cells (counting multiplicities). However a single occupied cell can satisfy multiple direction requirements of multiple dominos. So lower bound not straightforward.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712077792,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712078846,"data":"       | Maybe we can think of graph where each occupied cell can \"block\" up to how many direction requirements? For a cell, which direction sets include it? Let's compute.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712080242,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712081247,"data":"       | A cell can be part of many direction sets: For any domino adjacent to it in a particular direction.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712082476,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712083498,"data":"       | Specifically, a cell can block:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712084572,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712085596,"data":"       | - For a horizontal domino to its right: cell is left neighbor of that domino.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712086776,"data":"       | - For a horizontal domino to its left: cell is right neighbor.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712087953,"data":"       | - For a horizontal domino above: cell is one of up neighbor cells (if cell is above left or above right).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712089164,"data":"       | - For a horizontal domino below: similar.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712090266,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.7120913,"data":"       | - For a vertical domino above: cell is up neighbor.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712092421,"data":"       | - For vertical domino below: down neighbor.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712093561,"data":"       | - For vertical domino left/right: cell can be left neighbor (one of two) or right neighbor.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712094761,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712095788,"data":"       | Thus each cell can belong to many direction sets.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712096924,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712097952,"data":"       | Thus lower bound maybe small.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712099049,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.7121001,"data":"       | Maybe minimal m is 4? Let's try to construct manually.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712102749,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712103784,"data":"       | Goal: place few dominos such that each domino's directions are blocked.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712104961,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712106007,"data":"       | Idea: Use a 2x2 block of dominos forming a \"square\" shape.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712107191,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712108237,"data":"       | Consider placing four dominos forming a 2x2 square: two horizontal dominos on top row covering (1,1)-(1,2) and (1,3)-(1,4)? Not.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712109508,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712110556,"data":"       | Better: Place a 2x2 block of four cells covered by two dominos crossing? But dominos cannot overlap.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712111772,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712112819,"data":"       | Maybe we can place a 2x2 square of four cells covered by two dominos: one horizontal covering (i,j)-(i,j+1), one vertical covering (i,j)-(i+1,j). But they would overlap at (i,j). Not allowed.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712114196,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712115241,"data":"       | Thus need non-overlapping.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712116347,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71211771,"data":"       | Maybe we can use a \"ring\" of dominos around a central empty cell, each domino blocked by the central empty cell? Wait central empty cell cannot block because need occupied.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712119118,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712120149,"data":"       | Maybe we can use a configuration where each domino is adjacent to others on all sides.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712121355,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712122372,"data":"       | Consider a 2x3 rectangle tiled by three dominos: two vertical and one horizontal? Let's attempt to design.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712123596,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712124612,"data":"       | Let's attempt to brute force search for small m using Python but with smarter pruning: we can use SAT solver? Not.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712125854,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712126878,"data":"       | But we can use ILP via `pyscipopt`? Not.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712127969,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712128996,"data":"       | Maybe we can use `python-constraint` library? Not.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712130113,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712131174,"data":"       | Alternative: Use BFS over O_mask states with up to certain number of dominos. Since board has 49 cells, O_mask can be represented as 49-bit integer. Number of possible O_mask with up to k dominos is sum_{i=0}^k C(84,i) but many overlapping.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712132639,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712133737,"data":"       | But we can BFS over O_mask states adding one domino at a time, and keep only those O_mask where all placed dominos are blocked (i.e., all direction sets intersect O_mask). However we need to know which dominos are placed to evaluate direction sets. But we can compute condition based on O_mask alone? Not exactly because we need to know which dominos are present to know which direction sets to consider. However we can infer: any domino that could be placed within O_mask (i.e., both its cells in O_mask) could be considered placed or not. But we need to ensure that for each domino we actually placed, its direction sets intersect O_mask. If we consider all possible dominos within O_mask, we need to ensure there exists a selection (a tiling) such that each selected domino's direction sets intersect O_mask. This is like we need to find a perfect matching of O_mask where each edge's direction sets intersect O_mask. That's a more complex condition.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712137764,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712138821,"data":"       | Thus we need to consider placements explicitly.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712140002,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712141382,"data":"       | Maybe we can use MILP with pulp but not available. Could implement branch-and-bound ourselves.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712142579,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712143588,"data":"       | But maybe minimal m is small enough that we can brute force combinations with pruning.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712144752,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712145816,"data":"       | Let's try to generate all subsets of placements up to size 5 using recursion with pruning of overlap and direction satisfaction.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712147069,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712148121,"data":"       | We can generate combinations recursively: choose placements in order, maintain O_mask and list of placed placements. At each step, we can compute unsatisfied direction sets as before. If unsatisfied becomes empty, we have solution.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71214957,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712150632,"data":"       | We can prune heavily: if remaining placements (non-overlapping) cannot possibly cover all unsatisfied cells, prune.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712151868,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712152927,"data":"       | We can also compute lower bound on additional dominos needed: each new domino can cover at most 2 new cells, and can satisfy at most some number of unsatisfied sets. Hard.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712154245,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712155266,"data":"       | But we can attempt depth-first search limited to size up to maybe 6 or 7 and see if solution found.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712156464,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712157488,"data":"       | Let's implement recursion that tries placements in order (index increasing) to avoid duplicates.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712158711,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712159757,"data":"       | assistantanalysis to=python codedef search_limit(limit):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712160888,"data":"       |     best_solution = None\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712161971,"data":"       |     found=False\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712163032,"data":"       |     # precompute list of placements sorted maybe by something\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712164191,"data":"       |     placement_indices = list(range(len(placements)))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712165318,"data":"       |     # recursion\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712166398,"data":"       |     def recurse(start_idx, O_mask, unsat_masks, placed):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712167554,"data":"       |         nonlocal found, best_solution\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712170029,"data":"       |         if placed \u003e limit:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712171178,"data":"       |             return\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712172244,"data":"       |         if not unsat_masks:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712173313,"data":"       |             # solution found\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712174389,"data":"       |             found=True\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712175461,"data":"       |             best_solution = O_mask\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712176555,"data":"       |             print(\"Solution with\", placed, \"dominos\")\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712177801,"data":"       |             return True\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712178932,"data":"       |         # heuristic lower bound: need at least ceil(popcount of union of unsat_masks bits / 2) dominos? Because each domino adds at most 2 new cells.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712180204,"data":"       |         # compute union of unsatisfied cells\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712181672,"data":"       |         union_unsat = 0\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712182767,"data":"       |         for m in unsat_masks:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712183851,"data":"       |             union_unsat |= m\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712184941,"data":"       |         needed_cells = popcount(union_unsat)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712186066,"data":"       |         # each new domino adds at most 2 new cells, but may also cover cells already occupied; lower bound on additional dominos:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712187321,"data":"       |         min_additional = (needed_cells + 1) // 2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712188476,"data":"       |         if placed + min_additional \u003e limit:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712189606,"data":"       |             return False\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712190689,"data":"       |         # choose a requirement mask with smallest bits\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712191808,"data":"       |         min_idx = min(range(len(unsat_masks)), key=lambda i: popcount(unsat_masks[i]))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712192974,"data":"       |         req_mask = unsat_masks[min_idx]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712194066,"data":"       |         # iterate over cells in req_mask\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712195189,"data":"       |         bits=req_mask\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712196383,"data":"       |         while bits:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712197463,"data":"       |             lsb=bits \u0026 -bits\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712198659,"data":"       |             cell_idx=lsb.bit_length()-1\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712199763,"data":"       |             cell=(cell_idx//n, cell_idx%n)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712200884,"data":"       |             bits-=lsb\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712201939,"data":"       |             # try placements covering this cell, with index \u003e= start_idx to avoid permutations\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712203272,"data":"       |             for idx in cell_to_placements[cell]:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712204394,"data":"       |                 if idx \u003c start_idx:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712205542,"data":"       |                     continue\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712206632,"data":"       |                 cell_mask=placements_masks[idx]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712209626,"data":"       |                 if cell_mask \u0026 O_mask:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712210817,"data":"       |                     continue\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712211931,"data":"       |                 # new O\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712213011,"data":"       |                 new_O = O_mask | cell_mask\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712214263,"data":"       |                 # update unsatisfied\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712215376,"data":"       |                 new_unsat=[]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712216468,"data":"       |                 for m in unsat_masks:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712217593,"data":"       |                     if m \u0026 new_O:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712218714,"data":"       |                         continue\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712219832,"data":"       |                     new_unsat.append(m)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712220948,"data":"       |                 # add new dir masks from this placement\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712222151,"data":"       |                 for dm in placements_dir_masks[idx]:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712223371,"data":"       |                     if dm==0:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712224483,"data":"       |                         continue\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712225589,"data":"       |                     if dm \u0026 new_O:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712226724,"data":"       |                         continue\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712227814,"data":"       |                     new_unsat.append(dm)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712228928,"data":"       |                 # recurse\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712230216,"data":"       |                 if recurse(idx+1, new_O, tuple(new_unsat), placed+1):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.712231398,"data":"       |                     return True\n"}
