,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71323504,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713236072,"data":"       | When we add a domino, we must ensure its cells are not already occupied (matching property). Also its cells cannot be in forced set as \"must be empty\"? Actually forced set are cells that must be occupied, not empty. So they can be added as occupied later.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713237619,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713238638,"data":"       | Thus after adding domino, we update forced set: add external neighbor cells (if inside board) to forced set.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713239855,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71324089,"data":"       | If any cell in forced set is already occupied, that's fine (it satisfies requirement). If a forced cell is also part of the same domino? Not possible because external neighbor cells are distinct from domino cells.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713242302,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71324333,"data":"       | Now we continue.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713244407,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713245492,"data":"       | At any point, we can also decide to leave some cells empty; but we don't need to decide empties explicitly; we just need to ensure that after we have placed D dominoes, the forced set is a subset of occupied set (i.e., all forced cells are covered by some domino). If not, we could add more dominoes, but we limit to D.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713247052,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713248134,"data":"       | Thus for a given D, we need to find a set of D dominoes such that the union of their cells (size 2D) includes all forced cells derived from them.\n"}
