,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713257637,"data":"       | Also we need to ensure that forced cells can be paired into dominoes without conflict (matching). That's a more complex constraint; we can approximate by checking that forced_not_occupied cells can be matched within the remaining cells (including possibly cells already occupied? Actually they need to be matched with some neighbor not already occupied). We'll need to check existence of a matching covering forced_not_occupied cells within the remaining free cells.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713259463,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713260538,"data":"       | We can use a bipartite matching algorithm to test feasibility: treat remaining free cells as graph; we need to find a matching that covers all forced_not_occupied cells (each forced cell must be matched with a neighbor also free). This is a perfect matching problem for a subset.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713262047,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713263131,"data":"       | We can implement using networkx? Not available. But we can implement a simple maximum matching algorithm for bipartite graph (grid is bipartite). Use Hopcroft–Karp.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713264517,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713265616,"data":"       | We'll need to compute maximum matching on subgraph induced by free cells (including forced cells). If the maximum matching size \u003c (number of forced_not_occupied)/2 (since each forced cell must be matched), then prune.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713267061,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713268119,"data":"       | But we also need to consider that we have limited number of dominoes left; we need to be able to cover all forced cells plus possibly additional cells to reach total D.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713269466,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713270477,"data":"       | Thus we can prune heavily.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71327813,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713279187,"data":"       | Given board size 49, D maybe around 12-15, search may be feasible.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713280354,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713281418,"data":"       | Let's implement.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713282471,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713283522,"data":"       | assistantanalysis to=python codefrom collections import defaultdict, deque\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713284698,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713285732,"data":"       | # board dimensions\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713286809,"data":"       | R, C = 7, 7\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713287875,"data":"       | N = R*C\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71328893,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713289957,"data":"       | def idx(r,c):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713291,"data":"       |     return r*C + c\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713292065,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713293098,"data":"       | def rc(i):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713295645,"data":"       |     return divmod(i, C)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713296726,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713297741,"data":"       | # generate all possible domino placements (edges)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713298868,"data":"       | dominos = []\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713299916,"data":"       | for r in range(R):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713300983,"data":"       |     for c in range(C-1):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713302062,"data":"       |         a = idx(r,c)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713303125,"data":"       |         b = idx(r,c+1)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713304187,"data":"       |         # orientation horizontal\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713305269,"data":"       |         # external neighbors: left of a, right of b\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713306405,"data":"       |         left = idx(r,c-1) if c-1 \u003e=0 else None\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713307868,"data":"       |         right = idx(r,c+2) if c+2 \u003c C else None\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71330905,"data":"       |         dominos.append((a,b,'H', left, right))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713310147,"data":"       | for r in range(R-1):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71331123,"data":"       |     for c in range(C):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713312299,"data":"       |         a = idx(r,c)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71331336,"data":"       |         b = idx(r+1,c)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71331441,"data":"       |         # orientation vertical\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713315522,"data":"       |         up = idx(r-1,c) if r-1 \u003e=0 else None\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713317318,"data":"       |         down = idx(r+2,c) if r+2 \u003c R else None\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713318521,"data":"       |         dominos.append((a,b,'V', up, down))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71331964,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713320672,"data":"       | len(dominos)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713321851,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713322879,"data":"     [Code]:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713323924,"data":"       | from collections import defaultdict, deque\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713325022,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.713326127,"data":"       | # board dimensions\n"}
