,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71594078,"data":"     [Turn 12]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715941901,"data":"     [Reasoning] (4080 chars):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715943075,"data":"       | analysisIt found solution with 24 dominos (full tiling except one empty cell). That's trivial but not minimal.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715944393,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715945467,"data":"       | We need better heuristic to reduce m.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715946656,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715947779,"data":"       | Maybe minimal m is around 12? Let's try to use local search: start with random matching of size m, then try to improve.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715949088,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715950176,"data":"       | But we need to know lower bound.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715951328,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715952435,"data":"       | Observation: Each domino needs at least one occupied neighbor in each direction (if inside board). Since there are 4 directions, we need at least 4 occupied cells adjacent (maybe overlapping). However each occupied cell can serve for up to 4 dominos (if placed adjacent). So lower bound maybe around (4*m)/max_coverage. Not helpful.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715954149,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715955263,"data":"       | Maybe we can think about parity: board 7x7 has 49 squares, 25 black and 24 white (checkerboard). Dominos always cover one black and one white. So any set of dominos covers equal numbers of black and white squares. So occupied cells count is even, and black=white count among occupied cells. So m can be any integer up to 24.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715957007,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715958254,"data":"       | Now consider direction constraints: For a horizontal domino, the up pair are two cells of same color? Let's examine: On checkerboard, adjacent squares horizontally have opposite colors. The cells above them have same colors as original squares? Actually board coloring: (r+c) parity. For horizontal domino at (r,c)-(r,c+1): colors are opposite. The cells above (r-1,c) and (r-1,c+1) also opposite and same colors as original squares? Since parity flips with row shift: (r-1 + c) parity = (r+c-1) opposite of (r+c). So colors swap. So the pair above are opposite colors as well.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715960389,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715963162,"data":"       | Thus blocking constraints may involve cells of both colors.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715964417,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715965526,"data":"       | Potential minimal arrangement maybe like placing dominos in a \"cross\" shape leaving many empty cells but each domino blocked by at least one neighbor.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715966955,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715968043,"data":"       | Let's try to use MILP via brute force using Python's `pyscipopt`? Not available.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715969333,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715970417,"data":"       | Maybe we can use `python`'s `itertools.combinations` to generate subsets of edges of size m, but with early pruning using board covering constraints (non-overlap). Could generate all matchings of size m using algorithm for matchings enumeration that uses recursion with first free cell (as we did) but also early pruning using unsatisfied pairs bound. That may be enough for moderate m like 10.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715972265,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715973345,"data":"       | Our earlier search timed out for m up to 8 due to huge branching. But with pruning bound maybe it will prune earlier; we need to ensure bound is effective.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715974724,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715975811,"data":"       | Let's test search for m=10 with pruning bound and see runtime.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715977051,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715978187,"data":"       | assistantanalysis to=python codedef find_solution_m(m, timeout=20):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715979537,"data":"       |     import time\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715980671,"data":"       |     start = time.time()\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715981814,"data":"       |     result = None\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715982949,"data":"       |     def rec(start_edge, occupied_mask, placed_edges):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715984174,"data":"       |         nonlocal result\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715985305,"data":"       |         # early exit\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715986428,"data":"       |         if result is not None:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715987613,"data":"       |             return True\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715988755,"data":"       |         # prune bound\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715992985,"data":"       |         unsat = unsatisfied_pairs(placed_edges, occupied_mask)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715994257,"data":"       |         cells_needed = set()\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715995429,"data":"       |         for pair in unsat:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715996592,"data":"       |             for cell in pair:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715997757,"data":"       |                 if not ((occupied_mask\u003e\u003ecell)\u00261):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.715999039,"data":"       |                     cells_needed.add(cell)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.716000229,"data":"       |         lower_needed = ceil(len(cells_needed)/2)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.716001445,"data":"       |         if len(placed_edges) + lower_needed \u003e m:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71600271,"data":"       |             return False\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.716003913,"data":"       |         if len(placed_edges) == m:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.716006703,"data":"       |             if not unsat:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.7160079,"data":"       |                 result = list(placed_edges)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.716009104,"data":"       |                 return True\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.716010285,"data":"       |             else:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.716011426,"data":"       |                 return False\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.716012627,"data":"       |         # find first free cell\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.716013813,"data":"       |         for i in range(N):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.716014989,"data":"       |             if not ((occupied_mask\u003e\u003ei)\u00261):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.716016287,"data":"       |                 first_free = i\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.716017447,"data":"       |                 break\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.716018605,"data":"       |         else:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.716019743,"data":"       |             return False\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.716020904,"data":"       |         # try edges containing first_free\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.716022149,"data":"       |         for (a,b) in [(first_free, nb) for nb in neighbors[first_free] if not ((occupied_mask\u003e\u003enb)\u00261)]:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.716023558,"data":"       |             # ensure a\u003cb ordering to avoid duplicates? not needed\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.716024892,"data":"       |             new_mask = occupied_mask | (1\u003c\u003ca) | (1\u003c\u003cb)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.716026211,"data":"       |             placed_edges.append((a,b))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.716027399,"data":"       |             if rec(start_edge, new_mask, placed_edges):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.716028597,"data":"       |                 return True\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.716029737,"data":"       |             placed_edges.pop()\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.716030928,"data":"       |         return False\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.716032077,"data":"       |     rec(0,0,[])\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.716033216,"data":"       |     return result, time.time()-start\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.716034404,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.716035489,"data":"       | for m in range(1,13):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.716036634,"data":"       |     sol, t = find_solution_m(m)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71603779,"data":"       |     print(m, sol is not None, t)\n"}
