,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.716401913,"data":"       | For a horizontal domino occupying squares (i,j) and (i,j+1) (row i, columns j and j+1). It can slide left if squares (i,j-1) and (i,j) are empty (i.e., leftmost cell's left neighbor empty) and within board; also right slide if squares (i,j+1) and (i,j+2) empty. So to prevent sliding, at least one of left neighbor of left cell or right neighbor of right cell must be occupied (by another domino) or out of bounds (board edge). Actually need to block both left and right moves. So for a horizontal domino, we need either left neighbor occupied or out of board, and either right neighbor occupied or out of board. Both sides must be blocked. Similarly for vertical domino: need top neighbor occupied/out-of-board and bottom neighbor occupied/out-of-board.\n"}
