,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718482129,"data":"       | Potential minimal arrangement: place a single domino? No, then both sides are empty (except board edges). If placed at edge, one side is edge, other side empty -\u003e can slide toward empty side. So not allowed.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718485059,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71848612,"data":"       | Two dominos: maybe place them adjacent to each other such that each blocks the other? Example: place two horizontal dominos in same row, adjacent: first covering (i,1)-(i,2), second covering (i,3)-(i,4). Then for first domino, left side edge blocks left, right side cell (i,3) is occupied (by second domino). So first domino cannot slide left (edge) and cannot slide right (occupied). For second domino, left side cell (i,2) occupied (by first), right side cell (i,5) empty (unless edge). So second domino can slide right unless (i,5) edge? Not edge because column 5 not edge. So fails.\n"}
