,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718630436,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718631525,"data":"       | We can treat board cells as either empty or occupied by a domino. We'll assign dominos recursively, ensuring constraints for already placed dominos are satisfied (i.e., they have both sides blocked). However, a domino's neighbor cells may be occupied later, so we need to allow future satisfaction. So we need to enforce that at final configuration all dominos satisfy constraints.\n"}
