,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718825433,"data":"       | Let's attempt to implement a brute-force search using recursion, adding dominos one by one, and checking final condition.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718826669,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718827691,"data":"       | We can also use python's `itertools.combinations` to generate subsets of dominos up to certain size, but we can prune by checking that each cell is covered at most once.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718829118,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718830151,"data":"       | Given small board, we can perhaps enumerate all placements of up to, say, m=6 or 7 dominos. Number of ways to place k non-overlapping dominos on 7x7 board is limited. We can compute using recursion.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718832958,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718834028,"data":"       | Let's implement a recursive search that tries to place dominos up to limit m, exploring placements, and after placing exactly m dominos, check condition. Use pruning: if we cannot possibly satisfy condition for placed dominos due to missing neighbor cells that cannot be filled later (e.g., a domino's both neighbor cells are empty and not at edge, and there is no room to place another domino covering those cells later because they are already occupied or out of board). But we can postpone.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718835878,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718837093,"data":"       | Simpler: generate all placements of up to, say, 6 dominos and test condition after full placement; we can also generate placements of any size up to maybe 8. The total number of ways to place up to 8 dominos may be manageable.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718838514,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718839555,"data":"       | We need to count number of ways to place k non-overlapping dominos on 7x7 board. Upper bound: choose 2k cells out of 49, then pair them in adjacency ways. Not huge for k up to 6.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718840873,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718841919,"data":"       | We can implement recursion: maintain board occupancy boolean 7x7. At each step, find first empty cell, try placing a domino covering it with each neighbor (right or down) that is also empty, then recurse.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718843326,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718844337,"data":"       | We'll generate all placements of exactly k dominos and test condition.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718845488,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718846507,"data":"       | Let's implement and see minimal k that yields a valid configuration.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718847641,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718848695,"data":"       | assistantanalysis to=python codefrom functools import lru_cache\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718849853,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718851011,"data":"       | def generate_placements(k):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718852111,"data":"       |     # returns list of placements, each as list of domino tuples ((r,c),(r2,c2))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718853285,"data":"       |     n=7\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718854336,"data":"       |     board = [[0]*n for _ in range(n)]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718855437,"data":"       |     placements = []\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718856528,"data":"       |     def backtrack(start_cell, placed):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718857618,"data":"       |         if len(placed)==k:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718858692,"data":"       |             placements.append([d for d in placed])\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718859835,"data":"       |             return\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718860898,"data":"       |         # find next empty cell index linear\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718862018,"data":"       |         # start from start_cell index to avoid duplicates\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718863161,"data":"       |         for idx in range(start_cell, n*n):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718864278,"data":"       |             r = idx//n\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718865335,"data":"       |             c = idx%n\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718867758,"data":"       |             if board[r][c]==0:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71886888,"data":"       |                 # try horizontal\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718869981,"data":"       |                 if c+1\u003cn and board[r][c+1]==0:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718871146,"data":"       |                     # place\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718872218,"data":"       |                     board[r][c]=board[r][c+1]=1\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71887332,"data":"       |                     placed.append(((r,c),(r,c+1)))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718874508,"data":"       |                     backtrack(idx+1, placed)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718875611,"data":"       |                     placed.pop()\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718876701,"data":"       |                     board[r][c]=board[r][c+1]=0\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718877807,"data":"       |                 # try vertical\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718879073,"data":"       |                 if r+1\u003cn and board[r+1][c]==0:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71888023,"data":"       |                     board[r][c]=board[r+1][c]=1\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718881365,"data":"       |                     placed.append(((r,c),(r+1,c)))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718882488,"data":"       |                     backtrack(idx+1, placed)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718883583,"data":"       |                     placed.pop()\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718884659,"data":"       |                     board[r][c]=board[r+1][c]=0\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718885758,"data":"       |                 # after trying placements, also we could leave cell empty (skip)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718886943,"data":"       |                 # but we need to ensure we consider configurations where some cells stay empty.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718888163,"data":"       |                 # So we just continue without placing domino at this cell.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718889311,"data":"       |                 # However to avoid infinite loops, we must mark it as considered.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718890484,"data":"       |                 # We'll just continue loop; this effectively leaves cell empty.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718891803,"data":"       |                 # but we must also ensure we don't later try to place a domino covering this cell.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718893009,"data":"       |                 # Since we didn't mark it occupied, later recursion may consider it again.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718894187,"data":"       |                 # To avoid duplicates, we need to move start_cell forward.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718895338,"data":"       |                 # So we just continue loop without marking.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718896461,"data":"       |                 # That's fine because we will try other cells later.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71889764,"data":"       |                 # But we must ensure we don't later place a domino covering this cell after skipping.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718898834,"data":"       |                 # That's allowed because we may later decide to cover it with a domino starting from a later index (which could be this cell's neighbor).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718900143,"data":"       |                 # However if we skip this cell now, later we might place a domino covering it with neighbor that appears later in order (e.g., vertical from above cell that was earlier). That could cause duplicate configurations where same set of dominos generated in different orders.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718904474,"data":"       |                 # To avoid duplicates, we can enforce that we only place dominos where the first cell (r,c) is the smallest index among its two cells.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718905949,"data":"       |                 # That's already satisfied because we only try placements where (r,c) is the first empty cell we encounter.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718907241,"data":"       |                 # So it's okay.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.718908346,"data":"       |                 # Continue loop.\n"}
