,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71906931,"data":"       | We can use recursive search that also prunes early based on condition that placed dominos must have potential to be blocked later. But maybe we can use smarter enumeration: we can generate placements using backtracking but also limit board size.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719070758,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719071769,"data":"       | Alternatively, we can use MILP via `pyscipopt`? Not.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719072917,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719073942,"data":"       | Maybe we can use Python's `python-constraint`? Not.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719075073,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719076079,"data":"       | Better approach: Use SAT solver? Not.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719077161,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719078201,"data":"       | We can try to implement backtracking with pruning: after placing some dominos, we can check if any placed domino already has both neighbor cells empty and not edge, and those neighbor cells are already occupied by other dominos? Actually we need them to become occupied later. So we can allow empties.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719079789,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719080819,"data":"       | But enumeration still large.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719081903,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719082925,"data":"       | Maybe we can reason analytically to find minimal m.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719084039,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719085061,"data":"       | Let's think about parity and covering constraints.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719086204,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719087243,"data":"       | Observation: For each domino, its two neighbor cells (call them \"adjacent cells\" along its orientation) must be occupied or edge. Let's call those neighbor cells \"support cells\". For a horizontal domino covering cells (r,c) and (r,c+1), the support cells are (r,c-1) and (r,c+2). For vertical domino covering (r,c) and (r+1,c), support cells are (r-1,c) and (r+2,c).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719089018,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719090059,"data":"       | Thus each domino requires that both support cells are occupied (or edge). Edge cells are not occupied but count as support.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719091295,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719092447,"data":"       | Thus we can think of a set S of occupied cells (the domino cells). For each domino e in placement, its support cells must be subset of S ∪ Edge.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71909387,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719094912,"data":"       | Thus each support cell must be either edge or occupied. So we need to ensure that for each domino, its two support cells are either occupied or outside board.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719096201,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719097238,"data":"       | Thus we can view the occupied set S must be \"closed\" under support operation: for any domino in placement, the two cells at distance 2 from its cells along its orientation must be in S (or outside). This suggests that S must be a union of intervals of length at least 3 in each direction.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719099949,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719101046,"data":"       | Specifically, consider any row. If we have a horizontal domino at columns c,c+1, then columns c-1 and c+2 must be in S (unless out of board). So that forces a pattern: any occupied cell that is part of a horizontal domino forces its neighboring cells at distance 1 from the domino ends to be occupied as well (maybe part of other dominos). This can propagate.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719102681,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719103749,"data":"       | Thus the occupied set S must be such that for each maximal horizontal segment of occupied cells, its length must be at least 3 (since interior cells can be part of dominos, and ends need neighbor occupied). Similarly for vertical segments.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71910518,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719106222,"data":"       | Thus any occupied cell must be part of a segment of length at least 3 in its orientation direction (if it is part of a domino). However a cell could be part of a vertical domino but also be part of a horizontal segment of occupied cells (i.e., neighbor cells horizontally occupied but not part of same domino). That's okay.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719107792,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719108813,"data":"       | Thus minimal arrangement likely uses \"snake\" where each domino is part of a longer line of occupied cells of length at least 3, but we can share cells across lines? Not share because each cell belongs to exactly one domino.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719110287,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719111425,"data":"       | Thus each line of occupied cells (in a given orientation) must have length at least 3, and the cells are tiled by dominos (non-overlapping). For a line of length L, the number of dominos covering it is floor(L/2). For L odd, there will be one leftover cell not covered by a domino (but still occupied). That leftover cell can be part of a perpendicular line.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719113056,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719114076,"data":"       | Thus we can try to construct minimal configuration using a single line of occupied cells of length L covering many cells, with leftover cells used for other lines.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719115373,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719116438,"data":"       | Goal: minimize number of dominos = number of occupied cells /2. So we want to minimize occupied cells while satisfying constraints. Occupied cells must be at least something.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719117756,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719118769,"data":"       | We can attempt to find lower bound using counting arguments.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719119904,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71912097,"data":"       | Consider the board as graph of cells with edges horizontal/vertical adjacency. Our placement selects a matching (set of edges) such that each selected edge's two incident vertices have degree at least 2 in the \"support graph\"? Not exactly.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719122507,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719123526,"data":"       | Define for each cell v, its \"support neighbors\" are the cells two steps away in same row/col direction: left two, right two, up two, down two? Actually support cells for a domino are one step beyond its ends (distance 1 from end). For a cell that is part of a domino, the support cells are adjacent to the domino ends, which are distance 1 from the cell at the end? For interior cells of a longer segment, they are part of a domino and also have neighbor cells at distance 2 from the other end of the domino? Complexity.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71912765,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71912869,"data":"       | Maybe easier to brute force using ILP solver implemented ourselves using Python's `pyscipopt`? Not.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71912991,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719130918,"data":"       | But we can implement a simple MILP using `python-mip`? Not.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71913219,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719133311,"data":"       | We could implement a SAT solver using python's `python-sat`? Not.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719134488,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719135493,"data":"       | Alternative: Use exhaustive search with pruning for small m, maybe up to 8 or 9 dominos, to see if any configuration exists. Since board is 7x7, number of ways to place 8 dominos may be manageable with pruning.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71913689,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719138093,"data":"       | Let's implement recursive backtracking that enumerates placements up to certain m, but with early exit when find a valid configuration.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719139368,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71914038,"data":"       | We'll implement a function search(m, start) that tries to place m dominos; if we reach m placed, check validity; if valid, return arrangement.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719141646,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719142678,"data":"       | We'll also prune by checking that any placed domino already has both support cells occupied or edge (i.e., already satisfied). If not, we may still be able to satisfy later, but we can compute if there is enough remaining empty cells to fill those support cells later (i.e., they are not already occupied by other dominos and not out of board). That's okay.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719144284,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719145299,"data":"       | But the search space still large.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719146378,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719147379,"data":"       | We can also use heuristic: we can try to place dominos in a pattern like a snake.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719148544,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719149547,"data":"       | Maybe we can manually construct a minimal arrangement.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71915068,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719151716,"data":"       | Let's attempt to manually design.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719152805,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719153818,"data":"       | Idea: Use a \"U\" shape: vertical column of 3 dominos (cover rows 1-2,3-4,5-6) in column 0, leaving row0 empty. As we saw earlier, the topmost domino (rows1-2) needs cell (0,0) occupied. So we can place a horizontal domino covering (0,0)-(0,1). This occupies (0,0) and (0,1). Now check constraints:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71915543,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719156515,"data":"       | - Horizontal domino at (0,0)-(0,1): left neighbor edge blocked, right neighbor cell (0,2) must be occupied. Not yet.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719159337,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719160377,"data":"       | - Vertical domino rows1-2: top neighbor (0,0) now occupied (by horizontal), bottom neighbor (3,0) occupied (by second vertical). So blocked.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719161706,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719162856,"data":"       | - Second vertical domino rows3-4: top neighbor (2,0) occupied (by first vertical), bottom neighbor (5,0) occupied (by third vertical). Blocked.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719164129,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719165168,"data":"       | - Third vertical domino rows5-6: top neighbor (4,0) occupied (by second vertical), bottom neighbor (7,0) edge (since row7 out). So blocked.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719166466,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719167491,"data":"       | Now we need to block the horizontal domino's right neighbor (0,2). Could place vertical domino covering (0,2)-(1,2) perhaps, which would occupy (0,2) and (1,2). Let's see constraints:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719168845,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719170048,"data":"       | - Vertical domino (0,2)-(1,2): top neighbor edge (row -1) blocked, bottom neighbor (2,2) must be occupied. So need cell (2,2) occupied.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719171318,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71917235,"data":"       | - That could be a horizontal domino covering (2,1)-(2,2) maybe, etc.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719173507,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719174513,"data":"       | We can continue building.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719175589,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719176609,"data":"       | Goal: minimize total dominos.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719177704,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719178714,"data":"       | Let's try to implement a constructive approach using a \"spiral\" that fills cells such that each new domino blocks previous ones.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719180028,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719181062,"data":"       | Maybe minimal m is 7? Let's try to search using heuristic algorithm (like simulated annealing) to find a valid configuration with small m.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719182357,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719183403,"data":"       | We can treat problem as SAT: variables for each domino (horizontal/vertical) binary, constraints as earlier. Could use python's `pysat`? Not.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719184694,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719185701,"data":"       | But we can implement a simple local search: start with random set of dominos of size m, enforce non-overlap, then try to satisfy constraints by adding missing support cells using additional dominos (increase size). But we need minimal.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719187151,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719188187,"data":"       | Better: Use MILP via `scipy.optimize.linprog`? Not integer.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719189334,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719190372,"data":"       | Maybe we can implement branch and bound ourselves using recursion with constraints.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719191555,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719194093,"data":"       | Given small board, we can try to search for minimal m up to maybe 10 using recursion with pruning and early exit.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719195347,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71919641,"data":"       | We need to generate placements of m dominos (non-overlapping). Number of matchings of size m in a 7x7 grid? Could be large but maybe manageable for m up to 8.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719197724,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71919875,"data":"       | Let's attempt to implement recursion that chooses next empty cell and tries placing domino (right/down) or skip (leave empty). We'll also keep track of count of placed dominos; we stop when placed m dominos and remaining empty cells can't accommodate more (i.e., we have placed exactly m). At that point we test validity.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719200325,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719201385,"data":"       | To reduce branching, we can order cells and only place dominos when we decide to use them; we can also prune if remaining cells insufficient to reach m.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719202694,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719203867,"data":"       | Let's implement search for m from 1 upward, with early exit when find solution. Use recursion with backtracking.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719205098,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719206111,"data":"       | assistantanalysis to=python codedef find_solution(max_m=10):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719207264,"data":"       |     n=7\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719208334,"data":"       |     board = [[0]*n for _ in range(n)]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719209425,"data":"       |     # precompute neighbor positions for support checks\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719210565,"data":"       |     def is_valid_current(placed):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719211645,"data":"       |         # check all placed dominos that have both support cells already determined (occupied or edge)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719212856,"data":"       |         # but we may allow some support cells empty for now\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719214007,"data":"       |         # We'll just not prune here.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71921511,"data":"       |         return True\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719216167,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719217205,"data":"       |     # We'll implement recursion that tries to place exactly target_m dominos\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71921838,"data":"       |     def recurse(idx, placed, target_m):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719219509,"data":"       |         # idx linear index to consider\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719220591,"data":"       |         # placed list of dominos\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719221684,"data":"       |         # board occupancy global\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719222796,"data":"       |         # prune if placed count \u003e target_m\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719223941,"data":"       |         if len(placed) \u003e target_m:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719225098,"data":"       |             return None\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719226176,"data":"       |         # if we reached end of board\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719227269,"data":"       |         if idx \u003e= n*n:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719229877,"data":"       |             if len(placed) == target_m:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719231009,"data":"       |                 # check full validity\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719232106,"data":"       |                 if is_valid(placed):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719233186,"data":"       |                     return placed\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719234269,"data":"       |             return None\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719235339,"data":"       |         # compute remaining cells count\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719236453,"data":"       |         remaining_cells = n*n - idx\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719237591,"data":"       |         # max possible additional dominos we could place = remaining_cells//2\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719238824,"data":"       |         if len(placed) + remaining_cells//2 \u003c target_m:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719239983,"data":"       |             return None\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719241034,"data":"       |         r = idx//n\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719242101,"data":"       |         c = idx%n\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719243185,"data":"       |         if board[r][c]==0:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719244256,"data":"       |             # try placing horizontal domino\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71924536,"data":"       |             if c+1\u003cn and board[r][c+1]==0:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719246491,"data":"       |                 board[r][c]=board[r][c+1]=1\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719247623,"data":"       |                 placed.append(((r,c),(r,c+1)))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719248745,"data":"       |                 sol = recurse(idx+1, placed, target_m)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719249858,"data":"       |                 if sol:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719250916,"data":"       |                     return sol\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719252153,"data":"       |                 placed.pop()\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719253242,"data":"       |                 board[r][c]=board[r][c+1]=0\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719254343,"data":"       |             # try vertical domino\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719255433,"data":"       |             if r+1\u003cn and board[r+1][c]==0:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719256596,"data":"       |                 board[r][c]=board[r+1][c]=1\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719257691,"data":"       |                 placed.append(((r,c),(r+1,c)))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719258796,"data":"       |                 sol = recurse(idx+1, placed, target_m)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719259908,"data":"       |                 if sol:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719260955,"data":"       |                     return sol\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719262045,"data":"       |                 placed.pop()\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719263124,"data":"       |                 board[r][c]=board[r+1][c]=0\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719264216,"data":"       |         # skip this cell (leave empty)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719265318,"data":"       |         sol = recurse(idx+1, placed, target_m)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719266436,"data":"       |         if sol:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719267479,"data":"       |             return sol\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719268569,"data":"       |         return None\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719271331,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719272387,"data":"       |     for m in range(1, max_m+1):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719273476,"data":"       |         # reset board\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719274561,"data":"       |         board = [[0]*7 for _ in range(7)]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719275717,"data":"       |         sol = recurse(0, [], m)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71927679,"data":"       |         if sol:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719277846,"data":"       |             print(\"found solution with m=\", m)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719279021,"data":"       |             return m, sol\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719280119,"data":"       |     return None\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719281183,"data":"       | \n"}
