,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719372904,"data":"       | We can incorporate constraint checking early: For any placed domino, if its support cells are both determined (i.e., either edge or already occupied), we can check they are blocked; if any support cell is empty but could later be occupied, it's okay. However we can prune if a support cell is outside board (edge) or already occupied; if it's empty but there is no way to occupy it later because it's already past index? Actually we can still occupy later because we may place domino covering that cell later, as long as it's not already occupied.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719374855,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719375891,"data":"       | But we need to ensure that each empty support cell can be eventually occupied by some domino without overlapping existing placements. This is complex.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719377226,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719378245,"data":"       | Maybe we can use SAT solver via `python-sat` not available.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719379379,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719380445,"data":"       | Alternative: Use BFS over states of occupied cells, not placements. Since each domino occupies two cells, we can think of building occupied set S gradually, ensuring that for each domino in S (i.e., each pair of adjacent occupied cells that we intend to be a domino) we also need support cells.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719381943,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719382969,"data":"       | But we also need to decide orientation.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71938409,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719385136,"data":"       | Maybe we can use integer linear programming via `pyscipopt` not installed.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719386315,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719387321,"data":"       | Maybe we can use `z3`? Not installed.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719388459,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719390768,"data":"       | We can implement our own branch-and-bound with constraints as linear inequalities using `python` and `itertools` for small m.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719392038,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719393094,"data":"       | We can treat variables x_e for each possible domino (84). Use Python's `itertools.combinations` to iterate over subsets of size m, but prune using overlap condition quickly.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719394415,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719395461,"data":"       | We can generate all subsets of size m of dominos that are non-overlapping (matching). Number of matchings of size m may be less than total combos.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719396905,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719397932,"data":"       | We can generate all matchings of size m using recursion similar to earlier but only generate matchings of size exactly m, not all subsets.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719399196,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719400242,"data":"       | Our earlier recursion enumerated all matchings up to size m but also allowed skipping cells, leading to many possibilities. However we can prune by only exploring placements where we either place a domino covering the first empty cell or skip that cell but then we cannot later cover it because we skip it; that's okay because we may leave cells empty. But the number of matchings of size up to 8 may still be huge.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719401975,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719402999,"data":"       | Let's estimate: number of matchings of size k in a grid graph 7x7 (49 vertices). This number grows quickly but for k=5 maybe few million? Could be manageable.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719404308,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719405333,"data":"       | We can implement recursion that enumerates matchings of size exactly k, using standard algorithm: choose first free vertex, either leave it unmatched (skip) or match it with one of its free neighbors, then recurse. This enumerates all matchings (including those with unmatched vertices). For k small, we can prune when number of matched edges exceeds k.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719406941,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719407966,"data":"       | But we also need to consider that we can leave many vertices unmatched; we just need exactly k edges. So we can stop when matched edges count == k, and then we don't need to consider remaining vertices (they can stay unmatched). So recursion can stop early.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719409443,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719410447,"data":"       | Thus we can implement a function that selects edges up to target k, using backtracking, and when we have k edges, we test validity and return.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719411724,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719412734,"data":"       | We also need to ensure we don't generate duplicate matchings due to ordering; we can maintain a list of vertices not yet considered.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719413978,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719415156,"data":"       | Implementation: maintain a set of free vertices (cells). At each step, if we still need edges, pick a free vertex v (lowest index). Option 1: leave v unmatched, remove it from free set, continue. Option 2: for each neighbor u of v that is also free, add edge (v,u) to matching, remove both v and u from free set, recurse with edges+1.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719418473,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719419599,"data":"       | When edges count reaches target, we can stop and test.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719420717,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719421795,"data":"       | This should reduce search space because we only consider matchings up to size k, not all subsets of edges.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719423029,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719424057,"data":"       | Let's implement for k up to maybe 8 and see if we find solution.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719425198,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719426226,"data":"       | assistantanalysis to=python codefrom functools import lru_cache\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719427392,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719428405,"data":"       | n=7\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71942944,"data":"       | # map cell index to (r,c)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719430525,"data":"       | def idx_to_rc(idx):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719431625,"data":"       |     return divmod(idx, n)  # returns (r,c)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719432728,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719433833,"data":"       | def rc_to_idx(r,c):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719434913,"data":"       |     return r*n + c\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71943597,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719436991,"data":"       | # precompute neighbor indices for each cell (right, left, up, down)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719438168,"data":"       | neighbors = {}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719439215,"data":"       | for r in range(n):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719440273,"data":"       |     for c in range(n):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71944134,"data":"       |         idx = rc_to_idx(r,c)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719442478,"data":"       |         neigh = []\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71944368,"data":"       |         if c+1 \u003c n:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719444799,"data":"       |             neigh.append(rc_to_idx(r,c+1))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719445906,"data":"       |         if c-1 \u003e=0:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719447025,"data":"       |             neigh.append(rc_to_idx(r,c-1))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71944813,"data":"       |         if r+1 \u003c n:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719449242,"data":"       |             neigh.append(rc_to_idx(r+1,c))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719450328,"data":"       |         if r-1 \u003e=0:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71945142,"data":"       |             neigh.append(rc_to_idx(r-1,c))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719452543,"data":"       |         neighbors[idx]=neigh\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719453613,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719454626,"data":"       | # precompute support cells for each possible domino (edge)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71945577,"data":"       | # Represent domino as tuple (i,j) where i\u003cj and cells adjacent.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719456946,"data":"       | domino_support = {}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719458008,"data":"       | dominos = []  # list of (i,j) edges\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71945911,"data":"       | for i in range(n*n):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719461728,"data":"       |     r_i,c_i = idx_to_rc(i)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719463002,"data":"       |     # right neighbor\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719464073,"data":"       |     if c_i+1 \u003c n:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719471299,"data":"       |         j = rc_to_idx(r_i,c_i+1)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719472443,"data":"       |         if i\u003cj:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719473547,"data":"       |             dominos.append((i,j))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719474631,"data":"       |             # support cells: left of i, right of j\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719475783,"data":"       |             left = rc_to_idx(r_i,c_i-1) if c_i-1\u003e=0 else None\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719476981,"data":"       |             right = rc_to_idx(r_i,c_i+2) if c_i+2\u003cn else None\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719478185,"data":"       |             domino_support[(i,j)] = (left, right)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719479307,"data":"       |     # down neighbor\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719480365,"data":"       |     if r_i+1 \u003c n:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719481461,"data":"       |         j = rc_to_idx(r_i+1,c_i)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719482741,"data":"       |         if i\u003cj:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719483859,"data":"       |             dominos.append((i,j))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719484945,"data":"       |             # support cells: up of i, down of j\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719486049,"data":"       |             up = rc_to_idx(r_i-1,c_i) if r_i-1\u003e=0 else None\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.71948724,"data":"       |             down = rc_to_idx(r_i+2,c_i) if r_i+2\u003cn else None\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719488419,"data":"       |             domino_support[(i,j)] = (up, down)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719489545,"data":"       | \n"}
