,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719946449,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719947478,"data":"       | Let’s define for each domino D, count of directions where shift stays inside board. For a domino placed entirely interior (not touching any edge), all four directions are interior, so 4 requirements. If domino touches one edge, then that edge direction is blocked by board, so 3 requirements. If touches two adjacent edges (i.e., placed at corner), then two directions blocked, so 2 requirements. If touches opposite edges (i.e., spanning full length? Not possible because board 7). So maximum reduction is 2.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719949396,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719950436,"data":"       | Thus each domino contributes at least 2 requirements (if placed at corner). Each requirement must be satisfied by occupying at least one of the two target cells. A single occupied cell can satisfy multiple requirements (if it's a target for multiple dominos). So we need to cover all requirements with occupied cells.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.719952025,"data":"       | \n"}
