,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.720055347,"data":"       | Now each domino has up to 4 directions each requiring either 1 or 2 cells to be empty.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.720056528,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.720057555,"data":"       | Thus we can compute requirement counts: For a horizontal domino interior (not touching left/right edges), left and right each need 1 cell; up and down each need 2 cells. So total required cells = 1+1+2+2 = 6 cells (some may overlap across dominos). For a vertical interior domino: up/down 1 each, left/right 2 each =\u003e also 6.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.720059196,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.720060225,"data":"       | If domino touches left edge, left slide is blocked by board (no requirement). So reduces by 1.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.720061408,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.720062407,"data":"       | If touches top edge, up slide blocked (requires 2 cells but blocked). So reduces by 2.\n"}
