,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.720064635,"data":"       | Thus corner domino (touching left and top) would have left blocked (0), up blocked (0), right 1, down 2 =\u003e total 3 cells required.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.720065926,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.720066936,"data":"       | Thus each domino requires at most 6 cells to be occupied (or board) to block.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.720068111,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.720069406,"data":"       | Now each occupied cell can block multiple requirements. For a given cell, which sliding requirements does it satisfy? It can be one of the needed cells for sliding left/right (single cell) of a horizontal domino adjacent, or one of the two cells for vertical slide of horizontal domino, etc.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.720070948,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.720071978,"data":"       | Thus each cell can satisfy up to maybe 4 requirements (maybe more). Let's compute maximum: For a cell (r,c), consider all dominos that could slide into that cell as part of required empty cells. For horizontal domino sliding left, the required cell is the cell left of its leftmost cell. So a domino that has leftmost cell at (r,c+1) would need (r,c) empty. That domino occupies (r,c+1)-(r,c+2). So that domino's left slide requirement includes cell (r,c). Similarly horizontal domino sliding right requires cell right of rightmost cell: domino with rightmost cell at (r,c-1) would need (r,c). So that's another domino. For vertical slide up/down for vertical domino similar.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.720074118,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.720075157,"data":"       | Also for vertical slide of horizontal domino (up/down), both cells above (or below) must be empty; each of those cells could be (r,c). So a horizontal domino located at (r+1,c)-(r+1,c+1) sliding up requires cells (r,c) and (r,c+1) empty. So (r,c) is part of that requirement. Similarly sliding down for domino at (r-1,c)-(r-1,c+1). So each cell can be part of up to 4 two-cell requirements (as one of the two cells). So total maybe up to 8? Let's compute systematically later.\n"}
