,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.723278458,"data":"       | We can attempt to model as a covering problem: each domino occupies two cells. The board has 49 cells. Some cells may be empty. The condition for each domino: For each of four directions (N,S,E,W), at least one of the two cells that would be newly occupied after sliding in that direction must be either outside board or occupied by another domino (i.e., not empty). Since other dominos remain fixed, they block.\n"}
