,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724069669,"data":"       | analysisThe search for k up to 7 timed out after 30 seconds. We need to improve efficiency.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724070817,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724071805,"data":"       | We can incorporate some pruning: For each direction requirement, we need at least one cell occupied. So after selecting some placements, we could check for each placed domino if there exists any direction where required set is on-board and all cells are already blocked (i.e., cannot be occupied by future placements because they are already occupied by other placed dominos? Actually they could be occupied by other placed dominos already; if none occupied yet, but they could be occupied later. So we cannot prune.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724073586,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724074754,"data":"       | But we can incorporate heuristic ordering: choose placements that are more likely to block others (e.g., interior placements). Not sure.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724075938,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724076931,"data":"       | Alternatively, we can use MILP solver via `pyscipopt` not available. Could use `python`'s `itertools.combinations` but we need to filter non-overlap quickly.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724078156,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724079121,"data":"       | Maybe we can generate all packings of size k using algorithm for exact cover (DLX). But we can also use BFS enumerating placements with bitmask and using recursion but with early detection of impossible directions: For each placed domino, if a direction's required cells are off-board or already occupied, then direction satisfied; else if the required cells are still free but there are not enough remaining placements to occupy them (e.g., each remaining placement can cover at most 2 cells, but we need at least one of two cells). Hard.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724082683,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72408366,"data":"       | Maybe we can use integer programming via `sympy` linear programming? Not.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724084798,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724085769,"data":"       | Alternative: Use SAT solver via Python's built-in `python` library? Not.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724086923,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724087907,"data":"       | But perhaps minimal m is not too small; maybe it's 12 or more, making search for small k impossible; we need to find minimal m maybe larger.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724089104,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724090065,"data":"       | We can try to search for configurations using heuristic algorithm (e.g., random placement, then try to improve). Use local search: start with random set of dominos, ensure non-overlap, then check immobility; add dominos until condition satisfied; then try to remove some.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724091497,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724092461,"data":"       | We can use simulated annealing to find minimal m.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724093551,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724094537,"data":"       | But we need guarantee minimal; we can compute lower bound and then find construction achieving that bound.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724095673,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724096645,"data":"       | Let's think theoretically.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724097654,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724098631,"data":"       | We have 49 cells. Each domino occupies 2 cells. Some cells may be empty. For each placed domino, we need blocking cells for each direction. Counting constraints may give lower bound.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724099962,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724101056,"data":"       | Consider each direction requirement as a \"blocking need\". For each domino, there are up to 4 directions that need a blocking cell (if not blocked by edge). For each direction, we need at least one occupied cell among the required cells. The same occupied cell can serve as blocker for multiple dominos and multiple directions.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724102602,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724103568,"data":"       | Goal: minimize number of occupied cells (i.e., 2m cells). Since each domino occupies 2 cells, we want to minimize m, equivalently minimize number of occupied cells.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724104813,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724105797,"data":"       | Thus we can think of covering requirement: each placed domino D has a set of required cells (up to 4 sets). For each set, at least one cell must be occupied (by any domino). Equivalent to hitting set problem: we need to choose a set of occupied cells (those belonging to placed dominos) such that for each domino D and each direction d (with interior requirement), at least one of the required cells is in occupied set. Also the occupied cells must be partitionable into domino pairs (adjacent cells) forming dominos.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724108883,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724109854,"data":"       | Thus lower bound: each domino's required sets may be overlapping heavily.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724110972,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724111925,"data":"       | Maybe we can achieve configuration where each domino is blocked by its neighboring dominos that share edges, like a checkerboard arrangement.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724113122,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724114087,"data":"       | Potential minimal m might be 12 (occupying 24 cells). Let's try to search for any valid configuration using heuristic algorithm and see m.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724115265,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724116222,"data":"       | We'll attempt to use integer programming via `pyscipopt` not available; but we can use `python`'s `ortools`? Not installed.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724117388,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72411838,"data":"       | We can implement a constraint satisfaction solver using backtracking with pruning based on constraints as we add placements.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724119734,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724120689,"data":"       | We can also use SAT via `python` library `pysat` not installed.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72412176,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724122737,"data":"       | Maybe we can use `z3`? Not installed.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724123752,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724124706,"data":"       | Thus we need to code our own search but more efficient.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724125766,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724126975,"data":"       | Observation: The board is small; we can treat each cell variable: whether it's occupied (by a domino) and which neighbor it's paired with. This is a matching problem with constraints.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724128278,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724129268,"data":"       | We can treat each cell as either empty or part of a domino with a neighbor. Represent as a matching on grid graph (vertices = cells, edges = adjacency). Each domino corresponds to an edge selected. The matching must be such that for each selected edge (domino), for each direction (N,S,E,W), if sliding in that direction would keep both cells on board, then at least one of the cells that would be newly occupied must be incident to a selected edge (i.e., occupied). That means the neighbor cell must be matched (i.e., occupied). So requirement: For each selected edge e = (u,v) (adjacent cells), for each direction d (dx,dy) where sliding is possible (both new cells on board), at least one of the new cells must be incident to a selected edge (i.e., occupied). Equivalent to: In the grid graph, for each selected edge e, for each direction d, the \"frontier cells\" (the cells that would be newly occupied after sliding) must have at least one of them be matched (i.e., part of any selected edge). This is a local condition.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724131902,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724132855,"data":"       | Thus we can formulate as a constraint satisfaction problem on edges.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724133957,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724134897,"data":"       | We can attempt to use backtracking on edges.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724135939,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724138159,"data":"       | Number of edges in 7x7 grid: horizontal edges: 7 rows * 6 = 42; vertical edges: 6*7 = 42; total 84 edges (same as placements). So same.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724139372,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724140339,"data":"       | But we can incorporate constraints gradually: When we select an edge, we can mark its two vertices as occupied. For each direction, we can check if there is any chance to satisfy later.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72414161,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724142764,"data":"       | Potential pruning: If after placing some edges, there is a selected edge e such that for some direction d, both required cells are currently empty and also cannot be occupied later because they are isolated (i.e., no remaining edges can cover them). For a cell to be occupied later, it must be part of some edge that is still available (i.e., not already occupied). If both required cells are currently empty but each has no free neighbor (i.e., all incident edges already used or would conflict), then direction cannot be blocked, so prune.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724144582,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724145535,"data":"       | Thus we need to know for each empty cell, whether there exists any unused edge that could occupy it (i.e., pair with a neighbor that is also empty). This can be computed.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724146753,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724147712,"data":"       | Implement backtracking with ordering: choose next edge to consider (maybe first unused cell). Use recursion with branch: either place a domino covering that cell (choose one of its incident free edges) or leave it empty (if not needed). But we must ensure that any placed domino's constraints are satisfied eventually.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724149189,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724150144,"data":"       | Goal: minimize number of edges selected.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724151169,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724152127,"data":"       | We can use branch-and-bound: keep best solution found (minimum edges). At each node, if current selected count \u003e= best, prune.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724153331,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724154304,"data":"       | We can also compute lower bound: remaining empty cells could be at most matched in pairs, so minimal additional edges needed to satisfy remaining unsatisfied constraints maybe.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724155557,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724156499,"data":"       | But implementing this may be complex but doable.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724157572,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724158524,"data":"       | Given board small, we can attempt to use BFS search with pruning and bound.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724159627,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724160577,"data":"       | Alternatively, we can use MILP via `sympy` linear programming? Not.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724161657,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72416262,"data":"       | Maybe we can use `python`'s `pulp` library? Not installed.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724163687,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724164644,"data":"       | But we can install packages? Not sure if internet allowed. Usually not.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724165749,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724167959,"data":"       | We can implement our own ILP solver using branch-and-bound with linear relaxation? Not needed.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724169104,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724170075,"data":"       | Let's attempt to implement backtracking search for minimal m using recursion and bound.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724171202,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724172165,"data":"       | We'll represent board cells as indices 0..48.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724173211,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724174188,"data":"       | We'll maintain:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72417522,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724176181,"data":"       | - occupied_mask: bits of cells occupied.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724177234,"data":"       | - selected_edges: list of edge indices (placements).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724178289,"data":"       | - For each placed edge, we need to ensure constraints satisfied eventually.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724179394,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724180527,"data":"       | We'll also maintain for each placed edge e, a set of directions still unsatisfied (i.e., required cells not yet occupied). We'll update when new cells become occupied.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724181754,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724182704,"data":"       | If at any point a placed edge has a direction where required cells are both off-board (blocked) -\u003e satisfied automatically. If required cells are on board but at least one occupied, direction satisfied.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724184031,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724185032,"data":"       | If required cells are on board and both empty, we need to potentially occupy at least one later. So we keep track of unsatisfied directions.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724186215,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72418717,"data":"       | If later we fill both required cells with occupied cells (by other edges), direction becomes satisfied.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724188298,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724189244,"data":"       | If later we determine that it's impossible to occupy any of those required cells (because both cells become permanently unavailable), we prune.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724190445,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724191442,"data":"       | When a cell becomes permanently unavailable? That would be when we decide to leave it empty and also all its incident edges are not selected and cannot be selected later because they would conflict with already occupied cells? Actually a cell could be left empty, but later we could still occupy it by placing a domino covering it with a neighbor that is also empty (if not already occupied). So a cell is \"available\" as long as it is empty and at least one of its incident neighbor cells is also empty (i.e., there is a free edge). However if both neighbor cells are occupied or out of board, then cell cannot be occupied later.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724193465,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724194398,"data":"       | Thus we can compute for each empty cell the set of possible edges that could occupy it given current occupied cells.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724195548,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72419651,"data":"       | If a direction's required cells are both empty but each has zero possible edges (cannot be occupied), then direction impossible -\u003e prune.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724199442,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724200412,"data":"       | Implementation details:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724201405,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724202362,"data":"       | - Precompute adjacency list for each cell: neighbor cells (up/down/left/right) within board.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724203504,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724204664,"data":"       | - For each cell, possible edges that could be selected are those connecting it to a neighbor cell that is also empty (i.e., not occupied). So we need to know current occupied mask.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724205915,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724206874,"data":"       | - For each empty cell, if it has at least one empty neighbor, then it can still be occupied later.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724208021,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724209034,"data":"       | Thus for direction requirement set S (size 1 or 2). If any cell in S has at least one empty neighbor (including possibly the other cell in S? Actually S may contain two cells that are adjacent horizontally or vertically. If we occupy one of them, we need to also occupy its neighbor cell (the other cell of the domino). That neighbor could be any adjacent cell, not necessarily the other cell in S. So as long as there exists any empty neighbor for that cell, we could later place a domino covering it.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724210789,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724211743,"data":"       | Thus condition for possibility: For each cell in S, there exists at least one neighbor cell that is empty (i.e., not occupied) and not the same as the cell itself. If both cells in S have no empty neighbor, then impossible.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724213088,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724214043,"data":"       | Edge case: If a cell is empty but all its neighbors are occupied, then cannot be occupied later.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724215205,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72421617,"data":"       | Thus we can compute quickly.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724217192,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724218149,"data":"       | Now implement backtracking search with branch-and-bound.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724219219,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724220176,"data":"       | We'll need to order selection of edges to explore.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724221239,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724222201,"data":"       | Simplify: Use recursion that picks the next empty cell (lowest index) that still could be occupied (i.e., has empty neighbor). For each such cell, we have two choices: either leave it empty (i.e., never occupy) or place a domino covering it with one of its empty neighbors (choose neighbor). However leaving it empty may affect constraints of already placed dominos that need this cell as blocker. But we can still leave empty if other cell in requirement set will be occupied later.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724223929,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724225215,"data":"       | Thus we need to keep track of unsatisfied directions for each placed domino. When we decide to leave a cell empty permanently (i.e., we commit to never occupy it), we must check that for each unsatisfied direction that includes this cell, there is still another cell in that direction set that could be occupied later. If not, prune.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724228244,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724229224,"data":"       | But we may not know which cells will be permanently empty until end.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724230318,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724231328,"data":"       | Alternative approach: Use MILP solving via brute force enumeration of subsets of cells (occupied) of size 2m, then check if they can be paired into dominos (i.e., perfect matching on induced subgraph). That's also combinatorial.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724232682,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724233621,"data":"       | But maybe minimal m is relatively large, making search heavy.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72423472,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724235651,"data":"       | Let's try to use heuristic search to find a configuration with small m, then we can try to prove minimal.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724236796,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724237762,"data":"       | We'll use simulated annealing: start with random set of dominos (matching) of size m, check if constraints satisfied; if not, add dominos to satisfy unsatisfied directions; try to remove some.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724239058,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724240474,"data":"       | But we need guarantee minimal.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724242135,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724243495,"data":"       | Better: Use integer programming via `python`'s `pyscipopt` not available.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724244662,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724245614,"data":"       | Maybe we can use `python`'s `z3-solver`? Not installed.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724246658,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724247619,"data":"       | But we can attempt to use `python`'s `itertools.combinations` to generate all subsets of placements of size up to maybe 10, but we need to prune heavily using non-overlap early. We attempted for k up to 7 and timed out after 30 seconds. Maybe we can improve by using bitmask and early pruning of directions: we can compute for each placement its required cells sets; we can precompute for each placement the union of those required cells (size up to 8). Then we can early prune if after selecting some placements, there exists a placement whose required cells are all currently empty and also all those cells are not in the union of cells of remaining placements (i.e., cannot be occupied later). That's similar to earlier.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724249694,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72425066,"data":"       | But perhaps minimal m is larger than 7, maybe 8 or 9. Our search timed out for up to 7; maybe minimal is 8 or 9, which may be more feasible with improved search.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724251884,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724252829,"data":"       | Let's attempt to implement a smarter search using recursion with ordering and pruning.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724253935,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724255082,"data":"       | We'll precompute for each placement its required cells per direction (list of sets). We'll also precompute for each cell the list of placements that include that cell (i.e., placements that occupy that cell). This will help to know which placements could block a direction.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724257874,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724258857,"data":"       | During recursion, we maintain:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724259896,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724260844,"data":"       | - occupied_mask\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724261859,"data":"       | - selected placements list\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724262901,"data":"       | - unsatisfied directions list: for each selected placement, a set of directions still unsatisfied.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724264054,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724265034,"data":"       | When we add a new placement, we update unsatisfied directions for all selected placements (including new) by checking if any required cell becomes occupied.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724266278,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724267244,"data":"       | If after adding, any placement has a direction where required cells are all off-board (blocked) -\u003e remove from unsatisfied (already satisfied). If required cells are on board and at least one is occupied -\u003e satisfied. Else unsatisfied.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72426863,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724269628,"data":"       | Now we need to ensure that unsatisfied directions can still be satisfied later. For each unsatisfied direction of a placement, we need to check if there exists at least one cell in its required set that is still \"available\" to be occupied later (i.e., empty and has at least one empty neighbor). If none, prune.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724271804,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724272762,"data":"       | Also we can compute lower bound on additional placements needed: each unsatisfied direction may be satisfied by occupying at least one cell; each new placement occupies 2 cells, could potentially satisfy up to 4 directions (maybe). So we can compute simple bound: number of unsatisfied directions / 2 (since each new domino can block at most 2 directions? Actually a new domino can occupy up to 2 cells, each cell could be part of required set for multiple directions. Hard.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724274474,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724275437,"data":"       | But we can at least bound: we need at least ceil(unsatisfied_directions / 2) more placements? Not accurate but could help.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724276601,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72427757,"data":"       | Let's implement recursion with branch-and-bound and see if we can find minimal solution.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724278695,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724279939,"data":"       | assistantanalysis to=python codefrom functools import lru_cache\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724281145,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724282094,"data":"       | # Precompute neighbor cells for each cell\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724283148,"data":"       | neighbors = {}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724284146,"data":"       | for r in range(R):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724285147,"data":"       |     for c in range(C):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724286157,"data":"       |         idx0 = idx(r,c)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724287164,"data":"       |         neigh = []\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724288179,"data":"       |         if r\u003e0: neigh.append(idx(r-1,c))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724289286,"data":"       |         if r\u003cR-1: neigh.append(idx(r+1,c))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724292194,"data":"       |         if c\u003e0: neigh.append(idx(r,c-1))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724293279,"data":"       |         if c\u003cC-1: neigh.append(idx(r,c+1))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724294349,"data":"       |         neighbors[idx0] = neigh\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724295357,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724296355,"data":"       | # Precompute for each placement its required sets per direction (only those with on-board cells)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724297485,"data":"       | placements_req = []\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724298528,"data":"       | for p in placements:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724299567,"data":"       |     dir_req = {}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724300558,"data":"       |     for d, req_set in p['req'].items():\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72430163,"data":"       |         if req_set is None:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724302637,"data":"       |             continue\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724303648,"data":"       |         # ensure all cells in req_set are on board (they are)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724304727,"data":"       |         dir_req[d] = frozenset(req_set)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724305758,"data":"       |     placements_req.append(dir_req)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724306794,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724307776,"data":"       | # For each cell, list placements that occupy it\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724308811,"data":"       | cell_to_placements = {i: [] for i in range(N)}\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724309869,"data":"       | for i,p in enumerate(placements):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724310897,"data":"       |     for cell in p['cells']:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724311928,"data":"       |         cell_to_placements[cell].append(i)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724312961,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724313932,"data":"       | # For each cell, list placements that could occupy it (i.e., any placement that includes that cell)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724315171,"data":"       | # same as above.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724316187,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724317154,"data":"       | # Function to check if a cell is \"available\" to be occupied later given occupied_mask\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724318324,"data":"       | def cell_available(cell, occupied_mask):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724319354,"data":"       |     if (occupied_mask \u003e\u003e cell) \u0026 1:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724320504,"data":"       |         return False\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724321505,"data":"       |     # check if any neighbor is also empty (so a domino could be placed)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724322616,"data":"       |     for nb in neighbors[cell]:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724323624,"data":"       |         if ((occupied_mask \u003e\u003e nb) \u0026 1) == 0:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724324795,"data":"       |             return True\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724325799,"data":"       |     return False\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724326871,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724327919,"data":"       | # For a set of cells (size 1 or 2), check if at least one cell is available\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724330382,"data":"       | def any_cell_available(cell_set, occupied_mask):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724331457,"data":"       |     for cell in cell_set:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724332621,"data":"       |         if cell_available(cell, occupied_mask):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724333775,"data":"       |             return True\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724334788,"data":"       |     return False\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724335781,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724336767,"data":"       | # We'll implement recursive search with branch-and-bound\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724337831,"data":"       | best_solution = None\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724338828,"data":"       | best_m = 100  # large\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724339814,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724340761,"data":"       | # Sort placements maybe by number of required directions (more constraints first)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724341901,"data":"       | placement_order = list(range(len(placements)))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724343071,"data":"       | # compute number of interior directions (i.e., len of dir_req)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724344168,"data":"       | placement_dir_counts = [len(placements_req[i]) for i in placement_order]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724345261,"data":"       | # sort descending\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724346265,"data":"       | placement_order.sort(key=lambda i: -placement_dir_counts[i])\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724347358,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724348311,"data":"       | # Precompute for each placement the list of direction requirement sets\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724349461,"data":"       | placement_dir_sets = []\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724350474,"data":"       | for i in range(len(placements)):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724351537,"data":"       |     dir_sets = list(placements_req[i].values())\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724352579,"data":"       |     placement_dir_sets.append(dir_sets)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724353605,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724354574,"data":"       | # recursion\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724355559,"data":"       | def backtrack(start_idx, selected, occupied_mask, unsat_dirs):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724356635,"data":"       |     global best_solution, best_m\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72435765,"data":"       |     # unsat_dirs: list of (placement_idx, list of direction sets still unsatisfied)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724358762,"data":"       |     # compute lower bound: need at least ceil(len(unsat_dirs_total)/2) more placements?\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724359936,"data":"       |     # each new placement can occupy at most 2 cells, each cell could satisfy many unsat dirs.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724361084,"data":"       |     # We'll use simple bound: need at least ceil(num_unsat_dir_sets / 4) placements? Not sure.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724362211,"data":"       |     # We'll just use count of selected \u003e= best_m prune.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724363324,"data":"       |     if len(selected) \u003e= best_m:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724364395,"data":"       |         return\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724365385,"data":"       |     # If no unsatisfied directions (all satisfied) we have a valid solution\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724368752,"data":"       |     if not unsat_dirs:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724369781,"data":"       |         # valid solution found\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724370862,"data":"       |         best_solution = selected.copy()\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724371891,"data":"       |         best_m = len(selected)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724372915,"data":"       |         print(\"Found solution m =\", best_m)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724374089,"data":"       |         return\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724375109,"data":"       |     # Choose a placement to consider next: maybe the one with most unsatisfied directions?\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724376471,"data":"       |     # For branching, we can try to satisfy unsatisfied directions by adding placements that occupy required cells.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724377652,"data":"       |     # Choose a direction requirement that is currently unsatisfied.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724378741,"data":"       |     # Pick first unsatisfied direction set from unsat_dirs[0]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724379849,"data":"       |     # unsat_dirs is list of tuples (p_idx, [set1,set2,...]) where each set is a frozenset of cells needed.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724381005,"data":"       |     # We'll pick a cell from one of those sets to occupy next.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724382095,"data":"       |     # Choose the first unsatisfied direction set\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724383147,"data":"       |     p_idx, dir_sets = unsat_dirs[0]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724384204,"data":"       |     # pick the first unsatisfied direction set\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724385249,"data":"       |     target_set = dir_sets[0]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724386259,"data":"       |     # For each cell in target_set, try to occupy it by placing a domino covering that cell (and some neighbor)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724387411,"data":"       |     for cell in target_set:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724388452,"data":"       |         if (occupied_mask \u003e\u003e cell) \u0026 1:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724389631,"data":"       |             continue  # already occupied (should have satisfied)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.724390725,"data":"       |         # find possible placements that include this cell and do not overlap occupied cells\n"}
