,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.725718073,"data":"       | We can attempt to solve computationally: brute-force search for minimal m on 7x7 board. There are 49 squares, each domino occupies 2 squares. Number of possible placements of a domino is (horizontal placements: 7 rows * 6 columns = 42) plus vertical placements: 6 rows * 7 columns = 42, total 84 possible domino positions (edges). Choose subset of these placements such that they are non-overlapping (no square used by more than one domino). And condition holds.\n"}
