,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.725830111,"data":"       | analysisNow we need a function to check condition for a set of placements.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.7258313,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.725832325,"data":"       | Condition: For each domino d, orientation determines ends.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.725833467,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.725834522,"data":"       | If orientation H: cells leftmost = (r,c) (c smaller), rightmost = (r,c+1). For left end, adjacent cell to left is (r,c-1) if c\u003e0 else outside. For right end, adjacent cell to right is (r,c+2) if c+2\u003c7 else outside. Need that for each end, either outside (edge) or occupied by some domino (i.e., some placement covering that cell). Similarly for V orientation: up end adjacent cell above (r-1,c) if r\u003e0 else outside; down end adjacent cell below (r+2,c) if r+2\u003c7 else outside.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.725836478,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.725837497,"data":"       | Thus we need to know which cells are occupied by any domino in the set.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.725838665,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.725839682,"data":"       | Implementation: compute set of occupied cells. Then for each domino, check ends.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.725840847,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.725841882,"data":"       | Let's implement.\n"}
