,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.726332127,"data":"       | Better: Use recursion with ordering of cells to fill. Choose a cell that is not yet occupied but is required by some placed domino; then we must place a domino covering that cell. This ensures we satisfy constraints as we go.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.726333515,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.726334536,"data":"       | Algorithm:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.726335585,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.726336596,"data":"       | We maintain:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72633766,"data":"       | - occupied_mask\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.726338711,"data":"       | - list of selected placements\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.726339827,"data":"       | - required set: cells that must be occupied (due to adjacency of placed dominos) but are currently empty.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.726341056,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.726343613,"data":"       | Initially required set empty, selected empty.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.726344758,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.726345783,"data":"       | When we add a placement:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.726346855,"data":"       | - new_occupied = its cells.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.726347978,"data":"       | - For each adjacency cell of this placement (if within board), if not already occupied, add to required set.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72634923,"data":"       | - Also, some required cells may become satisfied because they are now occupied.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.726350397,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.726351618,"data":"       | Goal: find configuration where required set becomes empty (i.e., all adjacency requirements satisfied) after we finish placing placements (selected count = m). Additionally, we must ensure that after final placements, there are no unsatisfied required cells (they must be occupied). So at termination required set must be subset of occupied cells (which is automatically after we update). Actually we update required set after each addition; we also remove from required set any cells that become occupied.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.726353496,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72635452,"data":"       | Thus after each addition we keep required set = (required cells from all placed dominos) \\ occupied.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.726355835,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.726356901,"data":"       | Now we can prune: if size of required set \u003e 2*(target_m - len(selected)), then impossible because each future domino can at most occupy 2 new cells (but also may satisfy multiple required cells). However a domino could cover up to 2 required cells simultaneously, so bound may be tighter: each future domino can cover at most 2 required cells, so if required cells count \u003e 2*remaining placements, impossible. That's a valid prune.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.726358755,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.726359787,"data":"       | Also we need to ensure that we can place dominos that cover required cells without overlapping existing occupied cells. So we need to check that for each required cell, there is at least one placement that covers it and does not overlap occupied cells (including other required cells? Overlap not allowed with occupied but can cover other required cells simultaneously). So we can compute for each required cell, list of placements that cover it and are compatible with current occupied mask (i.e., placement mask \u0026 occupied_mask == 0). If any required cell has zero compatible placements, prune.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.726361852,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72636289,"data":"       | Also we need to consider that placements may also create new required cells (adjacent cells). So recursion may expand.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.726364115,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.726365121,"data":"       | We can also use heuristic: pick a required cell (or any empty cell) and try placements covering it.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72636634,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.726367348,"data":"       | We also need to enforce that we cannot exceed board edges; that's fine.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.726368529,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.726369704,"data":"       | Goal: find any solution with minimal m.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.726370803,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.726373381,"data":"       | We can try to search for m from lower bound upward, using recursion with pruning.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.726374605,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.726375634,"data":"       | Let's implement.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.726376699,"data":"       | \n"}
