,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727085688,"data":"       | analysisFor placement 0 (horizontal at row0 col0-1). Sliding left: target cells are (-, -1) and (0,0)?? Actually for cell (0,0) shift left gives (0,-1) out of board; for cell (0,1) shift left gives (0,0) inside. So inside list contains only cell index 0 (the original left cell). Since one target cell is outside board, slide is blocked automatically; we don't need condition. Indeed we only need constraints when both target cells inside.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727087467,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727088533,"data":"       | Thus for each placement d and direction dir where len(inside)==2, we require at least one other domino covering either of those cells.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727089831,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727090877,"data":"       | Now we can formulate search.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727091952,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727093012,"data":"       | We can attempt to solve via integer programming using python's pulp but not available. Could implement using python's MILP via OR-Tools? Might not be installed.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727094323,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727095375,"data":"       | Instead, we can brute force using BFS incremental: try to find configuration with m dominos satisfying constraints. Since minimal m likely small (\u003c10), we can search combinations of placements of size m, using pruning based on constraints.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72709683,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727098151,"data":"       | But number of combos for m=5: C(84,5)=~3.4 million. That's manageable with pruning maybe.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727099386,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72710046,"data":"       | We must also enforce non-overlap constraints. So we can generate all subsets of placements that are pairwise non-overlapping. That reduces combos.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727101743,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727102762,"data":"       | We can precompute adjacency: for each placement, set of cells it occupies (2). Overlap if intersection non-empty.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727104015,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727105063,"data":"       | We can generate all sets of placements with no overlap using backtracking. At each step, we can also check blocking constraints for already placed dominos? But blocking constraints involve other dominos possibly not yet placed, so we cannot guarantee until final set.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727106552,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727107588,"data":"       | Thus we can generate all non-overlapping subsets up to size k, then test blocking constraints at end.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727108808,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727109855,"data":"       | But number of non-overlapping subsets may still be large. However for small k maybe okay.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727112672,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727113742,"data":"       | Let's implement search for minimal m.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727114842,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727115879,"data":"       | We'll iterate m from 1 upwards, generate all combinations of placements of size m that are non-overlapping, test if each domino is blocked in all four directions.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727117172,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727118192,"data":"       | We need efficient overlap checking. Use bitmask representation: board has 49 cells, fits within 64-bit integer. Represent each placement as bitmask of its two cells.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72711953,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727120565,"data":"       | Let's compute bitmask for each placement.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727121663,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727122676,"data":"       | assistantanalysis to=python code# compute bitmask for each placement\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727123843,"data":"       | placement_masks = []\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727124928,"data":"       | for (c1,c2) in placements_cells:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727126033,"data":"       |     mask = (1 \u003c\u003c c1) | (1 \u003c\u003c c2)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727127224,"data":"       |     placement_masks.append(mask)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72712831,"data":"       | # verify\n"}
