,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727830485,"data":"     [Reasoning] (4253 chars):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727831568,"data":"       | analysisIt still finds 7 as best after many trials. Let's see if we can find 6.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72783274,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72783379,"data":"       | We'll run exhaustive search for m up to 6 using backtracking with pruning maybe feasible.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727835011,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727836051,"data":"       | We can attempt to generate all subsets of size up to 6 that are non-overlapping and test immobility.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727837274,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727838283,"data":"       | Number of non-overlapping subsets of size 6 might be large but perhaps manageable.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727839473,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727840488,"data":"       | We can generate all combinations of placements of size 6 and check overlap quickly using masks.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72784169,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727842688,"data":"       | C(84,6) ~ 300M, too many.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727843759,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72784476,"data":"       | But we can prune by ensuring non-overlap early using recursion.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727845887,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727847122,"data":"       | Let's implement depth-first search generating non-overlapping placements, limiting depth to 6, and test immobility when depth reached.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727848401,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727849465,"data":"       | We can also early prune using a heuristic: For each domino placed, we can compute number of directions that are already blocked (by edges or existing occupied cells). If at any point, even with all remaining empty cells, we cannot possibly block all directions for some domino because there are not enough remaining free cells to place blockers? Not straightforward.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727851102,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727852148,"data":"       | But we can try to implement recursion with pruning based on maximum possible additional blockers: each future domino can block at most 4 directions (maybe). For each placed domino we need each direction with both target cells inside to be blocked by at least one other domino; each direction corresponds to a pair of cells. If those cells are both currently free and not on edge, we need at least one future domino to occupy at least one of them. If we have limited remaining dominos (max depth 6) maybe we can compute lower bound.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727854072,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727855078,"data":"       | But maybe easier: we can use MILP but we can't.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727856184,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727857253,"data":"       | Alternative: Use Python's `itertools.combinations` but filter for non-overlap using bitwise quickly; we can generate combinations of size 6 using combination of masks and test overlap using bitwise OR.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727858648,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727859667,"data":"       | We can iterate over combinations using `itertools.combinations` but with early check: for combo, compute OR of masks and check if total bits count equals 2*len(combo). That ensures no overlap. This still requires iterating over all combos; 300M combos too many.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727862765,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727863805,"data":"       | But maybe number of non-overlapping combos of size 6 is far less than total combos because board only 49 cells; each domino uses 2 cells, so max dominos is 24. Number of ways to choose 6 non-overlapping placements may be less; we can compute via recursion.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727865277,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727866555,"data":"       | Let's write recursive enumeration with pruning: we maintain list of remaining placement indices that do not overlap current occupied mask. At each step, we iterate through those remaining indices, add one, recurse with updated mask and remaining list after that index (to avoid permutations). This enumerates each combination once.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727868152,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727869173,"data":"       | Complexity: number of ways to place 6 non-overlapping dominos on 7x7 board. Could be large but maybe manageable.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727870442,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727871492,"data":"       | Let's implement and stop early if we find any valid configuration with size \u003c=6.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72787273,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727873753,"data":"       | assistantanalysis to=python codedef find_solution_of_size(k, time_limit=30):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727874923,"data":"       |     import time, sys\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72787599,"data":"       |     start=time.time()\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72787707,"data":"       |     n=len(placements)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727878129,"data":"       |     # precompute list of placements that do not overlap each other? Not needed.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727879312,"data":"       |     # Use recursion\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727880385,"data":"       |     solution = None\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727881447,"data":"       |     def backtrack(start_idx, chosen, occ_mask):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727882576,"data":"       |         nonlocal solution\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727883649,"data":"       |         # prune if already found\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727884745,"data":"       |         if solution is not None:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727885829,"data":"       |             return\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727886903,"data":"       |         # if time exceeded\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72788801,"data":"       |         if time.time()-start \u003e time_limit:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727889134,"data":"       |             return\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.7278902,"data":"       |         if len(chosen)==k:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727891271,"data":"       |             # test immobility\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72789237,"data":"       |             if is_immobile(chosen):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727893478,"data":"       |                 solution = list(chosen)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72789457,"data":"       |             return\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727895619,"data":"       |         # Need to select more; iterate over remaining indices\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727896778,"data":"       |         for idx in range(start_idx, n):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727897885,"data":"       |             mask = placement_masks[idx]\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727901672,"data":"       |             if occ_mask \u0026 mask:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727902852,"data":"       |                 continue\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727903922,"data":"       |             # quick lower bound: remaining slots needed = k - len(chosen) - 1\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727905115,"data":"       |             # but we can also prune if not enough remaining placements after idx to fill\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727906316,"data":"       |             if n - idx \u003c k - len(chosen):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72790747,"data":"       |                 break\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727908562,"data":"       |             backtrack(idx+1, chosen+[idx], occ_mask|mask)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727909697,"data":"       |             if solution is not None:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727910805,"data":"       |                 return\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727911857,"data":"       |     backtrack(0, [], 0)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727912919,"data":"       |     return solution\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727913975,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727914988,"data":"       | for k in range(1,7):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727916278,"data":"       |     sol=find_solution_of_size(k, time_limit=10)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727917409,"data":"       |     print(k, \"solution:\", sol is not None)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727918583,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727919594,"data":"     [Code]:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727920628,"data":"       | def find_solution_of_size(k, time_limit=30):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727921736,"data":"       |     import time, sys\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727922823,"data":"       |     start=time.time()\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727923863,"data":"       |     n=len(placements)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727924908,"data":"       |     # precompute list of placements that do not overlap each other? Not needed.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727926096,"data":"       |     # Use recursion\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727927155,"data":"       |     solution = None\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.72792822,"data":"       |     def backtrack(start_idx, chosen, occ_mask):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.727929323,"data":"       |         nonlocal solution\n"}
