,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.728438852,"data":"       | Interpretation: We have a 7x7 board (grid of 7 rows, 7 columns). Place m dominos (size 1x2) covering two adjacent squares. We may place them anywhere; they can be oriented horizontally or vertically. The condition: No domino can slide horizontally or vertically when other dominos remain fixed. Means each domino is \"blocked\" from moving in its orientation direction? Actually sliding horizontally or vertically means translation along the board without rotating, moving whole domino to neighboring positions (like sliding one unit left/right/up/down) while other dominos stay where they are. The domino cannot slide because its path is blocked by other dominos or board edges.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.728441067,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.728442111,"data":"       | Specifically, a domino can slide horizontally if there is empty space to its left or right such that moving the domino one unit left/right (keeping orientation) results in covering squares that are currently empty (not occupied by other dominos) and still within board. Similarly vertical slide up/down.\n"}
