,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.728456915,"data":"       | Observation: For a domino to be immobile, at least one of its two squares must be adjacent to board edge in the direction of slide? Wait sliding along orientation axis: If domino is horizontal, sliding left or right. If it's at board edge, sliding further left would go off board, but sliding right may still be possible unless blocked. So to be immobile, both left and right moves must be blocked (by board edges or other dominos). Similarly vertical domino must be blocked both up and down.\n"}
