,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.730117107,"data":"       | Implementation steps:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.730118878,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.730119919,"data":"       | - Generate list domino_masks: integer bitmask for each domino (2 bits). Also neighbor list neighbor_masks? Actually neighbor cells may be multiple; we need to check each neighbor cell is either edge (outside board) or occupied by some domino in subset. So we can compute neighbor cell indices list; later we check for each neighbor index if that cell is occupied (i.e., mask has bit set). Since neighbor cell may be part of the same domino? No.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.730121697,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.730122715,"data":"       | Thus algorithm:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.730123766,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.730124791,"data":"       | For each subset of indices S of size m:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.730125904,"data":"       |     mask = 0\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.730126961,"data":"       |     for i in S:\n"}
