,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.731925274,"data":"       | Goal: each domino adjacent to two distinct dominos. In a graph of 4 vertices min degree 2, possible structures: cycle of length 4 (square). So we need four dominos arranged such that adjacency forms a cycle: D1 adjacent to D2 on left, D4 on right; D2 adjacent to D1 left, D3 right; D3 adjacent to D2 left, D4 right; D4 adjacent to D3 left, D1 right. This would correspond to a chain of four dominos arranged linearly, with ends also adjacent via the board edge? But need adjacency between D4 and D1 across board edges maybe using wrapping? Not possible.\n"}
