,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.73193755,"data":"       | One way is to place dominos in a \"ring\" shape around a 3x3 hole. For example, place dominos around perimeter of a 5x5 subboard: using alternating orientations to form a closed loop. Let's visualize.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.731939084,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.731940107,"data":"       | Consider a 5x5 region (rows 1..5, cols1..5). Place dominos along its border such that each domino's outward side (outside of the region) is occupied by another domino along the border. This could create a loop.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.731941529,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.731942559,"data":"       | Simplify: Use a \"zig-zag\" around a rectangle: Example: a 2x4 rectangle perimeter can be tiled by 4 dominos forming a loop: top edge two horizontal dominos, right edge vertical domino, bottom edge two horizontal dominos, left edge vertical domino. However overlapping at corners: need to ensure non-overlap.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.731944181,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.731945403,"data":"       | Let's attempt with 2 rows x 4 columns rectangle (rows 0,1 ; cols 0-3). Tiling possibilities: Top row: horizontal dominos covering (0,0)-(0,1) and (0,2)-(0,3). Bottom row: horizontal dominos covering (1,0)-(1,1) and (1,2)-(1,3). That's four dominos. But adjacency: top left domino right neighbor cell (0,2) occupied by top right domino, left neighbor off board (good). Bottom left domino right neighbor (1,2) occupied by bottom right domino, left neighbor off board. However vertical adjacency between top and bottom rows not needed because vertical dominos missing. For top left domino's down neighbor? Not required. Condition only cares about left/right, not up/down for horizontal domino. So bottom line not needed.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.731948919,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.731949995,"data":"       | Thus each horizontal domino's left/right neighbor satisfied except the rightmost domino's right neighbor (col4) off board? Actually top right domino covering (0,2)-(0,3): right neighbor col4 off board? No board width is 7; col4 is inside. So need column4 cell occupied. Not blocked. So fails.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.731951541,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.731952585,"data":"       | Thus need to extend to edge at rightmost side using vertical domino etc.\n"}
