,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.731954806,"data":"       | Thus maybe minimal m is larger.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.731955913,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.731956944,"data":"       | Maybe we can consider using board edges to block one side of each domino, thus each domino needs only one neighbor occupied (the side not at edge). That reduces requirement. If we can place dominos such that each domino touches board edge on one side (left/right/up/down) and the other side occupied by another domino, we might need fewer dominos.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.731958567,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.731959586,"data":"       | Thus we could place dominos along the border of the board. For each domino placed with one side against border, the border provides blocking for that side; we only need to block the other side by another domino.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.73196099,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.731962024,"data":"       | Thus we could arrange a chain of dominos along border, each touching border on one side, and each adjacent to next domino on its free side. At the end of chain, the free side would be at border also (if chain runs along border from corner to corner). But due to odd length, may have leftover.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.731963548,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.731964621,"data":"       | Let's attempt: place horizontal dominos along top row starting at left edge: first domino covering (0,0)-(0,1) left side off board, right side neighbor (0,2) must be occupied. Place second domino covering (0,2)-(0,3) left neighbor occupied by previous domino, right neighbor (0,4) need occupied; continue. To cover entire row with dominos, we need even number of cells. Since 7 columns odd, can't fill whole row with dominos; one cell remains uncovered, which would be needed to block last domino. Could use a vertical domino in that column to block.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.731966663,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.731967969,"data":"       | Thus we may need at least one extra domino to block the leftover.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.731969129,"data":"       | \n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":19207.731970158,"data":"       | Thus we can attempt to place dominos along all four sides, using vertical/horizontal combos to fill board edges with even number of cells, leaving maybe some cells to host extra dominos.\n"}
